1
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:54,001
[Welcome theme playing]

2
00:03:16,251 --> 00:03:19,834
[Welcome theme ends]

3
00:03:25,209 --> 00:03:28,083
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

4
00:03:28,084 --> 00:03:29,251
Triple welcome.

5
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:31,625
Basically, Welcome Three.

6
00:03:31,626 --> 00:03:33,458
Dubey, what's with all the drama?

7
00:03:33,459 --> 00:03:34,875
I was welcoming the Minister, sir.

8
00:03:34,876 --> 00:03:37,251
Ramprasad, what's up? All okay?

9
00:03:37,376 --> 00:03:38,833
- How's your party doing?
- All smooth.

10
00:03:38,834 --> 00:03:40,375
- Let's go get some tea.
- No, no tea.

11
00:03:40,376 --> 00:03:41,292
Hang on.

12
00:03:41,293 --> 00:03:42,208
You guys wait here.

13
00:03:42,209 --> 00:03:43,626
- I'll call you.
- Okay, Sir.

14
00:03:44,293 --> 00:03:46,000
Sinha, you're my only friend here.

15
00:03:46,001 --> 00:03:46,876
Since we were kids.

16
00:03:47,001 --> 00:03:48,918
- That's why I'm here to warn you.
- Yes.

17
00:03:49,584 --> 00:03:52,500
The opposition has its eyes
on businessmen like you

18
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:53,708
who "forget" to pay taxes.

19
00:03:53,709 --> 00:03:55,708
- So?
- So what?

20
00:03:55,709 --> 00:03:57,084
Elections are in three months.

21
00:03:57,293 --> 00:03:59,251
If we come back to power,
you can chill.

22
00:03:59,501 --> 00:04:00,417
I'm on your side.

23
00:04:00,418 --> 00:04:02,959
But if they win,
even I can't save you.

24
00:04:03,168 --> 00:04:04,250
You're serious, right?

25
00:04:04,251 --> 00:04:05,958
Figure out a fix
for all your tax evasions.

26
00:04:05,959 --> 00:04:08,751
Otherwise...
you are definitely "coming out."

27
00:04:09,584 --> 00:04:10,583
Coming out of where?

28
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:11,793
He'll first go in--

29
00:04:12,209 --> 00:04:13,376
For a very long time.

30
00:04:14,043 --> 00:04:14,918
Only then will he "come out."

31
00:04:15,626 --> 00:04:16,583
Take care.

32
00:04:16,584 --> 00:04:17,500
Think about it.

33
00:04:17,501 --> 00:04:18,500
Let's go.

34
00:04:18,501 --> 00:04:19,959
Dubey, this is serious.

35
00:04:20,126 --> 00:04:21,583
Call an emergency meeting.

36
00:04:21,584 --> 00:04:23,042
And get my daughter Jenny on board too.

37
00:04:23,043 --> 00:04:25,000
She's taken your jet to Paris.

38
00:04:25,001 --> 00:04:27,459
[suspenseful music]

39
00:04:31,626 --> 00:04:32,584
Ma'am.

40
00:04:35,459 --> 00:04:36,834
Oh Dad.

41
00:04:37,626 --> 00:04:38,543
Hi.

42
00:04:39,084 --> 00:04:40,000
Who is this?

43
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:41,333
It's Jenny here.

44
00:04:41,334 --> 00:04:42,459
It's not the phone, it's my hair.

45
00:04:42,626 --> 00:04:46,043
I got it dyed blonde in London.

46
00:04:46,668 --> 00:04:48,625
<i>I've called an emergency meeting.</i>

47
00:04:48,626 --> 00:04:50,000
<i>I've called my CA, my lawyer,</i>

48
00:04:50,001 --> 00:04:51,083
<i>my accountant, everyone.</i>

49
00:04:51,084 --> 00:04:52,001
So get here fast.

50
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:55,792
Are you making your will
in my name, Dad?

51
00:04:55,793 --> 00:04:58,376
Shut up and just get here.

52
00:04:58,793 --> 00:05:00,626
- Come on, baby. Let's go.
- [cat meows]

53
00:05:01,459 --> 00:05:04,083
So guys, here's the situation.

54
00:05:04,084 --> 00:05:06,833
I've got a tip from a very
special contact in the ministry.

55
00:05:06,834 --> 00:05:08,167
Who's this "special" contact, Dad?

56
00:05:08,168 --> 00:05:09,418
No, Jenny,

57
00:05:09,584 --> 00:05:11,876
I can't reveal his identity.

58
00:05:12,001 --> 00:05:13,625
You can't reveal his identity,

59
00:05:13,626 --> 00:05:14,543
but you can reveal his name.

60
00:05:14,668 --> 00:05:15,876
I just told you.

61
00:05:16,084 --> 00:05:17,376
You didn't say his name.

62
00:05:17,584 --> 00:05:19,458
I just said I cannot say his name.

63
00:05:19,459 --> 00:05:20,709
His name is Mr. Secret.

64
00:05:20,876 --> 00:05:22,459
Jenny, please.

65
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:23,542
Where were we?

66
00:05:23,543 --> 00:05:25,042
I was in Kanpur yesterday...

67
00:05:25,043 --> 00:05:26,708
for a hernia surgery.
That's why I missed my flight.

68
00:05:26,709 --> 00:05:27,708
I'm very sorry.

69
00:05:27,709 --> 00:05:28,876
Where was I?

70
00:05:29,043 --> 00:05:30,958
On "You can't reveal his identity."

71
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:32,917
Yes, I can't reveal Ramprasad's...

72
00:05:32,918 --> 00:05:34,083
[grits teeth angrily]

73
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,959
- What did I do?
- Jenny!

74
00:05:36,626 --> 00:05:39,084
[sips tea]

75
00:05:41,793 --> 00:05:44,333
So, guys, to get out of
this tax mess,

76
00:05:44,334 --> 00:05:47,918
we have to start a new business
where we officially show losses.

77
00:05:48,043 --> 00:05:52,375
Then we'll use those losses
to wipe out our old profits.

78
00:05:52,376 --> 00:05:53,958
Ideas. Come on, give me ideas.

79
00:05:53,959 --> 00:05:55,625
Let's start a heater factory

80
00:05:55,626 --> 00:05:56,750
for a super-hot place like Chennai.

81
00:05:56,751 --> 00:05:57,834
No one will buy it.

82
00:05:58,001 --> 00:05:59,000
Loss, loss, loss.

83
00:05:59,001 --> 00:06:00,043
Shut up!
Shut up!

84
00:06:00,584 --> 00:06:04,043
Dad, we'll build a 10-storey
buildings all over India,

85
00:06:04,168 --> 00:06:06,542
and put petrol pumps
on the 10th floor.

86
00:06:06,543 --> 00:06:07,918
No one will come.

87
00:06:08,043 --> 00:06:09,793
This is a stupid idea.

88
00:06:09,918 --> 00:06:11,333
All this will take years.

89
00:06:11,334 --> 00:06:13,959
We need something
we can start right now.

90
00:06:14,126 --> 00:06:15,751
[sips tea]

91
00:06:16,418 --> 00:06:18,333
Dubey... are you going
to keep slurping tea,

92
00:06:18,334 --> 00:06:19,709
or say something useful?

93
00:06:20,043 --> 00:06:22,043
In my view, sir,
you should make a film.

94
00:06:22,793 --> 00:06:24,584
What rubbish.

95
00:06:24,793 --> 00:06:28,543
Films are making crores these days.

96
00:06:28,918 --> 00:06:29,918
Like Dhurandhar.

97
00:06:30,084 --> 00:06:31,084
They do...

98
00:06:31,543 --> 00:06:34,458
but only the good ones.

99
00:06:34,459 --> 00:06:35,543
Made with real hard work.

100
00:06:35,668 --> 00:06:37,917
You have so many factories.

101
00:06:37,918 --> 00:06:40,792
You own the biggest jewellery store
in Dubai, Kanz.

102
00:06:40,793 --> 00:06:42,708
All that was built
with hard work and effort.

103
00:06:42,709 --> 00:06:45,292
In the same way,
we'll make a terrible film

104
00:06:45,293 --> 00:06:46,793
that definitely flops.

105
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:49,126
The income tax guys will be
stunned into silence.

106
00:06:50,001 --> 00:06:52,376
[silence]

107
00:06:52,918 --> 00:06:56,084
Dad, why does Dubey keep
losing his voice?

108
00:06:56,209 --> 00:06:59,208
When he was born, he was so dark,

109
00:06:59,209 --> 00:07:02,417
his father couldn't tell if it was
a baby or a lump of coal.

110
00:07:02,418 --> 00:07:03,543
He tried to strangle him.

111
00:07:03,709 --> 00:07:04,833
That's so sad.

112
00:07:04,834 --> 00:07:06,168
We'll show massive losses.

113
00:07:06,793 --> 00:07:08,293
Then we don't have
to fear the tax guys.

114
00:07:08,918 --> 00:07:11,918
Dubey...
imagine we make a film to flop,

115
00:07:12,793 --> 00:07:14,334
and somehow it becomes a hit?

116
00:07:14,459 --> 00:07:16,208
- No way that's happening.
- Why not?

117
00:07:16,209 --> 00:07:18,209
Because we won't cast mega-stars,

118
00:07:18,418 --> 00:07:19,833
we'll only cast background extras.

119
00:07:19,834 --> 00:07:20,708
How?

120
00:07:20,709 --> 00:07:23,417
Flop hero. Flop villain. Flop script.

121
00:07:23,418 --> 00:07:25,667
Flop technicians. Flop directors.

122
00:07:25,668 --> 00:07:27,792
And we'll blow up the budget.

123
00:07:27,793 --> 00:07:29,375
If they ask for a lakh,
we'll pay them in crores.

124
00:07:29,376 --> 00:07:30,875
If they ask for a crore,
we'll give them a hundred crore.

125
00:07:30,876 --> 00:07:31,792
That's it.

126
00:07:31,793 --> 00:07:32,918
- Dubey...
- Yes?

127
00:07:33,043 --> 00:07:34,168
Don't waste time.

128
00:07:34,543 --> 00:07:38,418
Find me a director
who can sink my ship.

129
00:07:38,543 --> 00:07:40,292
- Just like...
- Titanic?

130
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:41,126
Yes.

131
00:07:42,459 --> 00:07:44,542
I do know such directors.

132
00:07:44,543 --> 00:07:48,084
They are too big
even for Hollywood.

133
00:07:48,209 --> 00:07:50,708
Not one... but two directors.

134
00:07:50,709 --> 00:07:52,209
Ready.
Roll cameras.

135
00:07:52,376 --> 00:07:53,292
Action!

136
00:07:53,293 --> 00:07:54,334
And Rolling…

137
00:07:54,543 --> 00:07:57,625
This will be our first reel
that actually hits golden jubilee.

138
00:07:57,626 --> 00:07:58,751
[phone rings]

139
00:07:58,918 --> 00:08:00,168
Sorry, sorry... sorry.

140
00:08:01,543 --> 00:08:02,418
Who is it?

141
00:08:02,543 --> 00:08:03,583
Some Dubey is calling.

142
00:08:03,584 --> 00:08:04,334
Hello?

143
00:08:05,709 --> 00:08:06,584
Yes, okay.

144
00:08:06,918 --> 00:08:08,168
All right, done!

145
00:08:08,834 --> 00:08:09,668
What happened, Das?

146
00:08:09,876 --> 00:08:13,834
We just landed a brand-new
feature film to direct.

147
00:08:14,709 --> 00:08:16,001
My friend...

148
00:08:16,376 --> 00:08:17,959
Let him in too.

149
00:08:18,293 --> 00:08:20,793
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

150
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,793
Meet our directors

151
00:08:23,043 --> 00:08:24,668
Dev and Das.

152
00:08:29,709 --> 00:08:30,543
Hi.

153
00:08:30,793 --> 00:08:32,792
And this is our cameraman, Nainsukh.

154
00:08:32,793 --> 00:08:34,334
Hello.
Hello.

155
00:08:34,793 --> 00:08:36,668
Why does he have a thick lens
in just one eye?

156
00:08:38,459 --> 00:08:40,293
Because he can't see properly
with that eye.

157
00:08:40,418 --> 00:08:41,668
Then why not in the other one?

158
00:08:41,918 --> 00:08:43,793
No point.
He can't see at all with that eye.

159
00:08:44,626 --> 00:08:46,417
And his name is Nainsukh?

160
00:08:46,418 --> 00:08:48,292
Why do you even hire
a cameraman like this?

161
00:08:48,293 --> 00:08:50,500
- What can we do?
- We'll fire him if you want.

162
00:08:50,501 --> 00:08:51,793
You two want to fire me?

163
00:08:51,918 --> 00:08:53,458
I'll make your video go viral.

164
00:08:53,459 --> 00:08:55,418
He's really focused.
His eyesight is fine.

165
00:08:55,584 --> 00:08:56,708
What are you doing, Mr. Sinha?

166
00:08:56,709 --> 00:08:58,083
We need people like him.

167
00:08:58,084 --> 00:08:59,418
All right, fine.
Thank you.

168
00:08:59,543 --> 00:09:00,376
Thank you.

169
00:09:00,709 --> 00:09:01,959
Who is it?

170
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,168
Who's calling?

171
00:09:06,168 --> 00:09:07,209
Romeo bhai.

172
00:09:07,334 --> 00:09:08,418
Cut it. Hang up.

173
00:09:09,793 --> 00:09:12,834
How many films have you two made?

174
00:09:12,959 --> 00:09:14,334
Fourteen, sir.

175
00:09:14,543 --> 00:09:17,000
Out of their fourteen films,
fourteen were flops.

176
00:09:17,001 --> 00:09:18,043
And yet they are busy.

177
00:09:18,209 --> 00:09:19,501
I don't understand.

178
00:09:19,668 --> 00:09:20,583
I'll explain.

179
00:09:20,584 --> 00:09:23,750
There are two kinds of men
in this world.

180
00:09:23,751 --> 00:09:25,334
Those who can grow a beard

181
00:09:25,668 --> 00:09:27,918
and those who can't.

182
00:09:32,293 --> 00:09:33,501
- And...?
- And what?

183
00:09:33,668 --> 00:09:36,084
You said, those who can grow a beard

184
00:09:36,334 --> 00:09:37,584
and those who can't.

185
00:09:37,709 --> 00:09:39,043
- Exactly.
- What is that about?

186
00:09:39,251 --> 00:09:42,459
Those who can grow
a beard has two choices.

187
00:09:42,709 --> 00:09:45,751
They can either grow it
or shave it off.

188
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:49,876
But those who can't grow
a beard has no such choice.

189
00:09:50,376 --> 00:09:52,418
They can neither grow it nor shave it.

190
00:09:52,584 --> 00:09:54,000
Brilliant.

191
00:09:54,001 --> 00:09:56,209
The whole industry
knows he's the real deal.

192
00:09:56,334 --> 00:09:57,501
This is ridiculous.

193
00:09:57,751 --> 00:09:58,542
Thank you.

194
00:09:58,543 --> 00:10:00,251
Fine, I have a question.

195
00:10:00,376 --> 00:10:04,834
How much does it take
to make a good film?

196
00:10:05,043 --> 00:10:07,334
At least twenty thousand.

197
00:10:07,501 --> 00:10:11,626
But our budget...
is not twenty thousand.

198
00:10:12,001 --> 00:10:13,084
It's two thousand.

199
00:10:13,209 --> 00:10:15,375
Two thousand?

200
00:10:15,376 --> 00:10:19,417
You live like royalty,
and your budget is just two grand?

201
00:10:19,418 --> 00:10:20,751
Take it, take it, take it.

202
00:10:21,001 --> 00:10:22,001
Okay, Okay…

203
00:10:22,168 --> 00:10:26,043
But with only two thousand rupees,
the movie will be a--

204
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:27,626
Excuse me!

205
00:10:28,084 --> 00:10:30,001
It's not two thousand rupees.

206
00:10:30,626 --> 00:10:33,293
It's two thousand crore.

207
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:37,458
Two thousand crore rupees!

208
00:10:37,459 --> 00:10:39,293
Two thousand crore?

209
00:10:39,543 --> 00:10:41,417
Are you two serious about this?

210
00:10:41,418 --> 00:10:45,793
Look... people couldn't see
what I saw in your films.

211
00:10:46,168 --> 00:10:47,418
The second half of our film?

212
00:10:47,543 --> 00:10:50,834
No, I mean your hidden talents.

213
00:10:51,001 --> 00:10:53,584
With two thousand crore
we can hire Tom Cruise.

214
00:10:53,751 --> 00:10:56,500
The real one,
not Tom D'Souza from Santacruz.

215
00:10:56,501 --> 00:10:59,959
Since we're on the
topic of Tom Cruise...

216
00:11:00,168 --> 00:11:02,417
which is Tom Cruise's biggest hit film?

217
00:11:02,418 --> 00:11:03,375
Mission Impossible!

218
00:11:03,376 --> 00:11:04,584
And the director's name?

219
00:11:06,209 --> 00:11:08,668
Puzzled?
You don't know the director's name.

220
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,501
That's what I saw in you two.

221
00:11:10,668 --> 00:11:13,959
You can make stars out
of complete nobodies and...

222
00:11:14,293 --> 00:11:16,418
[silence]

223
00:11:16,834 --> 00:11:19,168
What happened to his voice?
I can't hear anything.

224
00:11:19,334 --> 00:11:21,751
It happens with him. When he
gets too excited, his voice just...

225
00:11:23,501 --> 00:11:26,208
The audience will cheer only one name:
Dev-Das.

226
00:11:26,209 --> 00:11:28,251
- [applause]
- Very nice. Very nice.

227
00:11:28,376 --> 00:11:31,583
There's just one more
thing I need to ask.

228
00:11:31,584 --> 00:11:33,459
Do you guys have a script?

229
00:11:33,584 --> 00:11:35,333
I've got this sure-shot
blockbuster plot.

230
00:11:35,334 --> 00:11:36,792
About a village deep in the jungle.

231
00:11:36,793 --> 00:11:39,376
Brave Indian soldiers go there

232
00:11:39,626 --> 00:11:44,083
and rescue the villagers
from deadly terrorists.

233
00:11:44,084 --> 00:11:45,250
What's the title?

234
00:11:45,251 --> 00:11:48,584
The title is... "Welcome to the Jungle."

235
00:11:48,709 --> 00:11:52,584
[hums the Welcome theme]

236
00:11:52,876 --> 00:11:56,459
Sign a flop hero fast and lock him in.

237
00:11:56,584 --> 00:11:57,834
I know just the guy...

238
00:11:58,001 --> 00:12:00,500
He was a top star once,
but now he's a complete flop.

239
00:12:00,501 --> 00:12:01,417
Really?

240
00:12:01,418 --> 00:12:02,917
These days, he's doing Bhojpuri films

241
00:12:02,918 --> 00:12:04,084
as an item boy...

242
00:12:04,334 --> 00:12:05,792
from slogging it out
to scrubbing it out.

243
00:12:05,793 --> 00:12:08,375
- One... Two ...Three... Four.
- <i>Scrub. Scrub.</i>

244
00:12:08,376 --> 00:12:11,833
<i>Scrub. Scrub.</i>

245
00:12:11,834 --> 00:12:12,750
Hello.

246
00:12:12,751 --> 00:12:13,667
- Hi.
- Hi.

247
00:12:13,668 --> 00:12:14,583
I'm Benny.

248
00:12:14,584 --> 00:12:17,000
- Broker?
- No, Rajeev sir's manager.

249
00:12:17,001 --> 00:12:20,084
<i>♪ Scrub, scrub… ♪</i>

250
00:12:20,251 --> 00:12:21,500
<i>♪ Scrub, scrub… ♪</i>

251
00:12:21,501 --> 00:12:23,834
<i>♪ With a soap, my love ♪</i>

252
00:12:24,793 --> 00:12:25,876
<i>♪ My love... ♪</i>

253
00:12:28,251 --> 00:12:29,167
<i>♪ My love... ♪</i>

254
00:12:29,168 --> 00:12:30,708
<i>♪ Scrub, scrub… ♪</i>

255
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:34,083
<i>♪ You grind my heart like ♪
♪ A millstone in your arms ♪</i>

256
00:12:34,084 --> 00:12:37,751
<i>♪ Sting on the lips like a bee ♪</i>

257
00:12:38,001 --> 00:12:40,458
<i>♪ Come closer, naughty girl ♪</i>

258
00:12:40,459 --> 00:12:44,417
<i>♪ I grind your heart like ♪
♪ A millstone in my arms ♪</i>

259
00:12:44,418 --> 00:12:47,793
<i>♪ Sting on the lips like a bee ♪</i>

260
00:12:47,959 --> 00:12:51,583
<i>♪ After luring me ♪
♪ With your sweet temptations ♪</i>

261
00:12:51,584 --> 00:12:54,250
<i>♪ Don't walk away now, my love ♪</i>

262
