Done. Done.

512
00:23:17,918 --> 00:23:19,418
Let me finish.

513
00:23:20,376 --> 00:23:23,251
Another fifty before we finish shooting.

514
00:23:24,084 --> 00:23:26,126
You mean fifty plus fifty plus fifty...

515
00:23:26,459 --> 00:23:27,501
that's one hundred and fifty.

516
00:23:27,626 --> 00:23:30,126
- Are you okay with that?
- Absolutely. Sit down.

517
00:23:30,251 --> 00:23:31,876
[whooshing]

518
00:23:32,126 --> 00:23:32,959
Oh, this is...

519
00:23:34,834 --> 00:23:35,834
- Brother?
- Yes.

520
00:23:36,001 --> 00:23:37,417
Can you hear anything?

521
00:23:37,418 --> 00:23:38,417
No.

522
00:23:38,418 --> 00:23:39,709
How did he lose his voice?

523
00:23:40,126 --> 00:23:41,708
Who cares.

524
00:23:41,709 --> 00:23:43,709
Let him lose his voice,
but we can't lose this deal.

525
00:23:43,834 --> 00:23:46,043
Hold on, hold on. Let me speak.

526
00:23:46,209 --> 00:23:47,583
I'm the producer's daughter.

527
00:23:47,584 --> 00:23:50,334
Fifty, fifty,
fifty-two hundred, done.

528
00:23:50,501 --> 00:23:52,875
- Two hundred.
- Two hundred. Two hundred.

529
00:23:52,876 --> 00:23:54,293
Get up now, you dog.

530
00:23:54,793 --> 00:23:56,292
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

531
00:23:56,293 --> 00:23:57,876
- Thank you, thank you.
- Yes. It's done. Come here, Chotu.

532
00:23:59,168 --> 00:24:00,751
[Welcome theme playing]

533
00:24:01,709 --> 00:24:02,543
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

534
00:24:02,668 --> 00:24:04,500
<i>♪ To the jungle welcome ♪</i>

535
00:24:04,501 --> 00:24:05,417
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

536
00:24:05,418 --> 00:24:07,083
<i>♪ Everyone, come welcome ♪</i>

537
00:24:07,084 --> 00:24:08,042
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

538
00:24:08,043 --> 00:24:09,667
<i>♪ To the party, come welcome ♪</i>

539
00:24:09,668 --> 00:24:12,168
<i>♪ Welcome-welcome-welcome ♪</i>

540
00:24:15,251 --> 00:24:18,501
[Welcome theme ends]

541
00:24:22,751 --> 00:24:24,126
[yawns]

542
00:24:24,459 --> 00:24:26,168
[phone rings]

543
00:24:26,334 --> 00:24:27,209
Who's calling?

544
00:24:28,793 --> 00:24:30,043
Romeo Bhai's.

545
00:24:30,376 --> 00:24:31,543
- Cut it.
- Damn.

546
00:24:32,043 --> 00:24:34,501
Calling during my chill time...

547
00:24:34,709 --> 00:24:36,001
[text notification]

548
00:24:36,209 --> 00:24:37,126
[eerie music]

549
00:24:37,251 --> 00:24:38,251
Whose text is it?

550
00:24:38,543 --> 00:24:39,542
Romeo bhai's.

551
00:24:39,543 --> 00:24:40,501
What does it say?

552
00:24:41,418 --> 00:24:42,459
"You're dead."

553
00:24:42,668 --> 00:24:43,834
[text notification]

554
00:24:44,043 --> 00:24:44,959
Whose text is it?

555
00:24:45,084 --> 00:24:46,418
Romeo bhai's.

556
00:24:46,543 --> 00:24:47,542
What does it say?

557
00:24:47,543 --> 00:24:48,459
"You're also dead."

558
00:24:50,084 --> 00:24:51,501
[phone ringing]

559
00:24:51,959 --> 00:24:53,751
[Romeo] Hey,
Smallpox, you hung up on me.

560
00:24:53,876 --> 00:24:55,043
Give the phone to Das.

561
00:24:56,709 --> 00:24:58,917
Hey, loser, getting too cocky, huh?

562
00:24:58,918 --> 00:24:59,959
Romeo bhai...

563
00:25:01,043 --> 00:25:03,625
How can we hear you
without picking up your call?

564
00:25:03,626 --> 00:25:05,292
Put it to your ear.

565
00:25:05,293 --> 00:25:06,418
Where are you?

566
00:25:07,709 --> 00:25:08,793
Behind you.

567
00:25:10,293 --> 00:25:12,168
- Romeo bhai?
- Put the phone to your ear.

568
00:25:14,709 --> 00:25:16,334
You guys weren't lifting my calls.

569
00:25:17,501 --> 00:25:19,918
Now these boys will lift you.

570
00:25:20,376 --> 00:25:21,584
Give them a lift.

571
00:25:22,543 --> 00:25:24,709
[action music]

572
00:25:25,501 --> 00:25:27,500
There is no GPS, so how will we go?

573
00:25:27,501 --> 00:25:28,793
Can't see anything.

574
00:25:29,626 --> 00:25:32,751
- [suspenseful music]
- [helicopter whirring]

575
00:25:40,626 --> 00:25:43,084
[suspenseful music continues]

576
00:25:46,418 --> 00:25:47,833
Meet Yeda Anna.

577
00:25:47,834 --> 00:25:49,334
He's permanently out of control.

578
00:25:49,459 --> 00:25:51,376
Do you know
what his brother used to say?

579
00:25:51,543 --> 00:25:52,751
"Control."

580
00:25:53,084 --> 00:25:54,543
"Control, Uday."

581
00:25:55,084 --> 00:25:56,333
And that's Romeo.

582
00:25:56,334 --> 00:25:57,250
Shortest fuse in the business...

583
00:25:57,251 --> 00:26:00,043
but he learnt how to add colour
to life from his brother.

584
00:26:00,209 --> 00:26:01,459
Majnu bhai.

585
00:26:02,584 --> 00:26:06,583
Their whole business is running
their brothers' business in India.

586
00:26:06,584 --> 00:26:09,918
Ransom, land-grabbing, extortion.

587
00:26:10,876 --> 00:26:12,918
[donkey screeching]

588
00:26:13,376 --> 00:26:16,418
That's Majnu bhai's painting.

589
00:26:16,876 --> 00:26:18,626
Brings back memories.

590
00:26:19,543 --> 00:26:21,584
You call that a painting?

591
00:26:21,751 --> 00:26:23,084
A donkey sitting on a horse.

592
00:26:23,251 --> 00:26:24,459
Let me show you my painting.

593
00:26:24,668 --> 00:26:25,501
Bring it.

594
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,834
This is what you call a painting.

595
00:26:28,043 --> 00:26:29,417
Masterpiece.

596
00:26:29,418 --> 00:26:31,168
A horse sitting on a donkey.

597
00:26:31,584 --> 00:26:32,751
Different concept.

598
00:26:33,293 --> 00:26:35,167
Never seen a sequel
in painting before.

599
00:26:35,168 --> 00:26:36,750
- Yes...
- And look at the detailing.

600
00:26:36,751 --> 00:26:38,708
Brilliant... look at the cuts, Anna.

601
00:26:38,709 --> 00:26:40,958
Wise guy, that reminds me.

602
00:26:40,959 --> 00:26:42,375
You were cutting his calls,
weren't you?

603
00:26:42,376 --> 00:26:43,876
No, no...

604
00:26:44,001 --> 00:26:44,917
No...

605
00:26:44,918 --> 00:26:45,917
You two didn't cut the call.

606
00:26:45,918 --> 00:26:48,167
Fine, let's talk about that.

607
00:26:48,168 --> 00:26:49,083
About what?

608
00:26:49,084 --> 00:26:52,459
That black thing you always carry.

609
00:26:53,459 --> 00:26:54,293
Him?

610
00:26:55,668 --> 00:26:58,834
No... the thing you put on your ear.

611
00:26:59,001 --> 00:27:00,542
- Earrings.
- Not earrings.

612
00:27:00,543 --> 00:27:03,668
We'll lose our memory trying to jog his.

613
00:27:03,793 --> 00:27:04,750
Hey...

614
00:27:04,751 --> 00:27:06,375
Last night you ordered food.

615
00:27:06,376 --> 00:27:07,292
How did you do it?

616
00:27:07,293 --> 00:27:09,750
One slap across the face
and food was delivered.

617
00:27:09,751 --> 00:27:10,793
No, no...

618
00:27:10,918 --> 00:27:13,750
We always do this.
We do this and then this.

619
00:27:13,751 --> 00:27:16,083
- Phone, Anna.
- Exactly.

620
00:27:16,084 --> 00:27:17,167
No one understands me.

621
00:27:17,168 --> 00:27:19,083
You cut his phone, wise guy.
Now pick up your phone.

622
00:27:19,084 --> 00:27:20,458
- Whose phone is ringing?
- Your phone's ringing.

623
00:27:20,459 --> 00:27:21,918
- Pick it up.
- Come on.

624
00:27:22,626 --> 00:27:24,668
Anna... isn't it weird?

625
00:27:25,001 --> 00:27:26,917
Talking on the phone
when we're right here.

626
00:27:26,918 --> 00:27:29,208
Not weird at all. Carry on.

627
00:27:29,209 --> 00:27:30,209
Hey, Smallpox,

628
00:27:30,334 --> 00:27:32,209
why's your phone down?
Put it to your ear.

629
00:27:32,334 --> 00:27:33,168
Can you hear me?

630
00:27:33,501 --> 00:27:34,958
I can hear you right here, bhai.

631
00:27:34,959 --> 00:27:36,293
Soon you'll hear me even louder.

632
00:27:37,376 --> 00:27:38,334
Only one bar.

633
00:27:38,543 --> 00:27:39,876
My phone's battery is low.

634
00:27:40,376 --> 00:27:41,293
Is it?

635
00:27:41,459 --> 00:27:42,625
Mine's got four.
Now talk.

636
00:27:42,626 --> 00:27:43,959
Why is your phone down again?

637
00:27:45,376 --> 00:27:46,209
Where's our money?

638
00:27:46,334 --> 00:27:48,209
Hello?

639
00:27:48,543 --> 00:27:50,792
Network issue, bhai.

640
00:27:50,793 --> 00:27:53,793
- Come here, come here.
- Yes, bhai.

641
00:27:54,543 --> 00:27:56,168
You'll get full network here.

642
00:27:56,293 --> 00:27:57,751
You'll hear everything.

643
00:27:58,168 --> 00:27:59,083
Where's our money?

644
00:27:59,084 --> 00:28:02,417
Technically,
you should be paying us, bhai.

645
00:28:02,418 --> 00:28:04,334
Not the other way round.

646
00:28:04,709 --> 00:28:05,626
Why are you crying?

647
00:28:05,793 --> 00:28:07,418
Trying to con Yeda Anna?

648
00:28:07,584 --> 00:28:10,375
Who calls so many times
for 2.5 lakh rupees?

649
00:28:10,376 --> 00:28:11,708
It's not about 2.5 lakhs.

650
00:28:11,709 --> 00:28:14,250
We burn that much just
on helicopter fuel.

651
00:28:14,251 --> 00:28:15,917
It's about reputation, got it?

652
00:28:15,918 --> 00:28:17,793
Uday bhai and Majnu bhai's reputation.

653
00:28:17,959 --> 00:28:19,833
Their reputation
is worth only 2.5 lakhs?

654
00:28:19,834 --> 00:28:22,667
You're lucky we're talking on the phone.

655
00:28:22,668 --> 00:28:24,251
If we were face-to-face,
I'd have rearranged your face.

656
00:28:24,376 --> 00:28:26,708
You're right.
I got lucky because of the phone.

657
00:28:26,709 --> 00:28:27,625
You're right.

658
00:28:27,626 --> 00:28:29,793
We're going to make millions, bhai.

659
00:28:30,001 --> 00:28:31,793
We're making a big film.
Try to understand.

660
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:35,001
We're giving a chance to new artists.

661
00:28:35,209 --> 00:28:37,293
- Bhai...
- Anna, can we talk in private?

662
00:28:37,418 --> 00:28:39,584
Anna, they're making a film.

663
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:41,501
And giving a chance to newcomers.

664
00:28:41,668 --> 00:28:43,583
We should be the heroes of this film.

665
00:28:43,584 --> 00:28:45,251
- Me too.
- Hundred percent.

666
00:28:47,293 --> 00:28:50,293
Why are you two smiling?

667
00:28:50,459 --> 00:28:53,043
Put your phones away.
We don't want your money.

668
00:28:53,376 --> 00:28:54,209
Then what do you want?

669
00:28:54,334 --> 00:28:55,458
The same thing you want.

670
00:28:55,459 --> 00:28:56,417
What do we want?

671
00:28:56,418 --> 00:28:58,084
The same thing your film wants.

672
00:28:58,209 --> 00:28:59,168
What does the film want?

673
00:28:59,293 --> 00:29:01,543
Fresh, talented artists.

674
00:29:01,668 --> 00:29:03,084
New artists?

675
00:29:03,418 --> 00:29:05,751
- Where are they?
- Right in front of you.

676
00:29:06,084 --> 00:29:08,417
All I see is a horse and a donkey.

677
00:29:08,418 --> 00:29:10,334
[donkey brays]

678
00:29:10,501 --> 00:29:11,834
- Why, you...
- Take aim, boys.

679
00:29:12,043 --> 00:29:15,543
By artists, I mean... us.
I mean us.

680
00:29:15,918 --> 00:29:19,667
Oh, Dev, what a face!

681
00:29:19,668 --> 00:29:21,418
What a personality!

682
00:29:21,626 --> 00:29:23,167
- Wonderful.
- Yeah.

683
00:29:23,168 --> 00:29:25,168
But I've got one request.

684
00:29:25,334 --> 00:29:28,792
No one should find out you two are dons.

685
00:29:28,793 --> 00:29:31,250
Otherwise the rest
of the cast will get scared.

686
00:29:31,251 --> 00:29:32,375
Don't worry at all.

687
00:29:32,376 --> 00:29:35,918
We'll act so well,
no one will even know we're acting.

688
00:29:36,418 --> 00:29:39,083
Even if we scream at you,
don't mind it.

689
00:29:39,084 --> 00:29:40,583
Take your phones out.
Take your phones out.

690
00:29:40,584 --> 00:29:42,958
But everything's sorted now.

691
00:29:42,959 --> 00:29:45,875
Take a selfie with the future stars.

692
00:29:45,876 --> 00:29:46,792
- Yeah, right.
- Selfie.

693
00:29:46,793 --> 00:29:47,751
Don't be scared.

694
00:29:47,876 --> 00:29:49,251
[camera shutter clicking]

695
00:29:50,418 --> 00:29:52,001
Fifty crores signing amount!

696
00:29:52,209 --> 00:29:53,501
Now that's what I call destiny.

697
00:29:53,668 --> 00:29:56,626
Why are you doing this flop
producer's film in a fake wig?

698
00:29:56,959 --> 00:29:57,918
Let it be.

699
00:29:58,251 --> 00:30:01,209
If my luck's finally shining,
why should I eclipse his?

700
00:30:01,584 --> 00:30:04,209
Maybe his luck will shine too
if I finish his film.

701
00:30:05,168 --> 00:30:07,459
It's all written in destiny.

702
00:30:08,668 --> 00:30:12,251
Destiny is what snatched me
from my father years ago.

703
00:30:13,626 --> 00:30:15,417
Major Vishwajeet Raj Kohli.

704
00:30:15,418 --> 00:30:16,500
[emotional music]

705
00:30:16,501 --> 00:30:21,168
One day, my father went on a mission
for India and vanished.

706
00:30:21,834 --> 00:30:23,876
He's been missing in action
for fifteen years.

707
00:30:24,334 --> 00:30:25,834
No one knows
what happened to him.

708
00:30:26,293 --> 00:30:28,501
Let's bury the past.
What's the latest?

709
00:30:29,001 --> 00:30:31,043
I forgot to tell you something, brother.

710
00:30:31,209 --> 00:30:33,751
Dev-Das have signed two more heroes.

711
00:30:34,293 --> 00:30:35,501
Anna and Romeo.

712
00:30:36,251 --> 00:30:37,667
And you're telling me this now?

713
00:30:37,668 --> 00:30:38,751
I just found out.

714
00:30:39,001 --> 00:30:39,834
Call him!

715
00:30:40,043 --> 00:30:42,751
[phone rings]

716
00:30:43,834 --> 00:30:44,668
Yes, Rajeev.

717
00:30:44,793 --> 00:30:46,834
You said I was the solo hero.

718
00:30:46,959 --> 00:30:47,876
Who are the other two?

719
00:30:48,043 --> 00:30:50,168
They're just fillers, Rajeev.

720
00:30:50,418 --> 00:30:51,626
Just dogs.

721
00:30:51,918 --> 00:30:53,084
You're the elephant.

722
00:30:53,709 --> 00:30:54,793
Say that again.

723
00:30:54,918 --> 00:30:55,751
All right.

724
00:30:56,168 --> 00:30:57,167
You're the elephant,

725
00:30:57,168 --> 00:30:59,751
they're the dogs barking
behind you.

726
00:31:01,168 --> 00:31:02,542
They're just dogs.

727
00:31:02,543 --> 00:31:04,084
[phone rings]

728
00:31:04,293 --> 00:31:05,543
Romeo bhai.

729
00:31:07,793 --> 00:31:08,708
Hello.

730
00:31:08,709 --> 00:31:10,209
Hey, Miniature.

731
00:31:10,709 --> 00:31:14,250
Heard you signed some actor called
Rajeev as hero.

732
00:31:14,251 --> 00:31:17,084
He's your dog.
You're the elephant.

733
00:31:17,251 --> 00:31:18,418
[laughter]

734
00:31:18,709 --> 00:31:19,793
All right, all right.

735
00:31:20,668 --> 00:31:21,709
Just a dog.

736
00:31:21,834 --> 00:31:24,626
[inspirational music]

737
00:31:24,876 --> 00:31:25,959
Welcome, Minister sir.

738
00:31:26,126 --> 00:31:27,668
Since you came,
everything's been a mess

739
00:31:27,793 --> 00:31:28,626
Blessing.

740
00:31:28,751 --> 00:31:30,418
Sorry, I meant a blessing.

741
00:31:30,918 --> 00:31:32,543
Thakur has assembled an army of idiots.

742
00:31:32,751 --> 00:31:33,876
[laughing]

743
00:31:34,293 --> 00:31:37,084
[intriguing music]

744
00:31:39,709 --> 00:31:40,709
Hi.

745
00:31:42,751 --> 00:31:44,501
Hello.

746
00:31:45,543 --> 00:31:47,334
Why don't you sign
my daughter as the heroine?

747
00:31:47,793 --> 00:31:50,834
If she's in the film, it'll surely flop.

748
00:31:51,001 --> 00:31:53,500
Jenny as the heroine.
Great idea.

749
00:31:53,501 --> 00:31:54,584
Super Hit.

750
00:31:54,709 --> 00:31:55,751
Oh Dubey!

751
00:31:55,876 --> 00:31:57,376
Me? A heroine?

752
00:31:57,543 --> 00:31:59,209
I am that talented.

753
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,209
Das, she's our heroine.

754
00:32:01,876 --> 00:32:03,584
Go, narrate her the scene.

755
00:32:03,959 --> 00:32:05,168
Please, please, please.

756
00:32:05,584 --> 00:32:07,834
- Go narrate it to her.
- You see...

757
00:32:07,959 --> 00:32:10,084
Let's go over there.
The other artists are waiting.

758
00:32:10,209 --> 00:32:11,043
- Okay, let's go.
- Come.

759
00:32:11,209 --> 00:32:14,043
[upbeat music]

760
00:32:19,918 --> 00:32:21,043
They have come.

761
00:32:21,418 --> 00:32:22,584
- Rajeev?
- [camera shutters clicking]

762
00:32:23,168 --> 00:32:25,084
Did you send money
to the paparazzi?

763
00:32:25,418 --> 00:32:27,501
Yes, to every single one.

764
00:32:27,793 --> 00:32:30,876
[Welcome theme playing]

765
00:32:32,293 --> 00:32:33,376
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

766
00:32:34,918 --> 00:32:36,209
Our hero Rajeev.

767
00:32:36,543 --> 00:32:39,833
You guys... how do you always
know where to pop up?

768
00:32:39,834 --> 00:32:41,167
Sir, you called us.

769
00:32:41,168 --> 00:32:42,083
Yeah...

770
00:32:42,084 --> 00:32:44,083
These fools take my money
and expose me.

771
00:32:44,084 --> 00:32:44,959
I won't spare them.

772
00:32:45,084 --> 00:32:47,501
Why did you invite
so many paparazzi?

773
00:32:48,126 --> 00:32:49,834
Meet our producer, Mr. Sinha.

774
00:32:50,168 --> 00:32:51,250
Pleasure.

775
00:32:51,251 --> 00:32:53,584
- Meet my friend, the Minister.
- Okay.

776
00:32:53,709 --> 00:32:54,834
Ramprasad.

777
00:32:55,543 --> 00:32:57,376
And look...
our other heroes are here too.

778
00:32:58,334 --> 00:32:59,334
Other heroes?

779
