1046
00:43:20,001 --> 00:43:20,918
Start sound.

1047
00:43:21,126 --> 00:43:22,918
Cameras.
Action!

1048
00:43:24,543 --> 00:43:26,543
[upbeat music]

1049
00:43:28,418 --> 00:43:30,418
[shouting]

1050
00:43:31,251 --> 00:43:32,501
- Brother!
- He's dead.

1051
00:43:33,001 --> 00:43:34,042
[gasps]

1052
00:43:34,043 --> 00:43:35,376
Sir, the jeep's flipped.

1053
00:43:35,501 --> 00:43:36,500
Which jeep?

1054
00:43:36,501 --> 00:43:38,042
[tense music]

1055
00:43:38,043 --> 00:43:38,958
He's dead.

1056
00:43:38,959 --> 00:43:41,001
Wasn't your brother an action star?

1057
00:43:41,751 --> 00:43:43,959
[intriguing music]

1058
00:43:44,543 --> 00:43:45,876
He won't die easily.

1059
00:43:46,043 --> 00:43:48,501
Yes, my brother is still an action star.

1060
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:51,209
[suspenseful music]

1061
00:43:54,793 --> 00:43:57,376
[suspenseful music continues]

1062
00:44:01,209 --> 00:44:03,209
[explosion]

1063
00:44:06,876 --> 00:44:08,917
Two seconds later
and he would've been dead.

1064
00:44:08,918 --> 00:44:09,876
Rascal.

1065
00:44:10,418 --> 00:44:11,293
It's really hot.

1066
00:44:11,418 --> 00:44:13,292
Hot? You're feeling hot?

1067
00:44:13,293 --> 00:44:14,209
Dubey!

1068
00:44:14,834 --> 00:44:15,833
Yeah! Yes.

1069
00:44:15,834 --> 00:44:17,584
Our heroine is feeling hot.

1070
00:44:17,709 --> 00:44:19,209
Are you serious?

1071
00:44:19,418 --> 00:44:21,708
Get the fan going. Turn it on.

1072
00:44:21,709 --> 00:44:23,583
[helicopter blades whirring]

1073
00:44:23,584 --> 00:44:25,667
I wanted a fan, not a tornado.

1074
00:44:25,668 --> 00:44:28,000
Big heroine, big fan.

1075
00:44:28,001 --> 00:44:28,833
Let's go!

1076
00:44:28,834 --> 00:44:29,792
[comic music]

1077
00:44:29,793 --> 00:44:32,125
So, Dubey,
What's the update on the shoot?

1078
00:44:32,126 --> 00:44:35,750
Sir, shooting's in full swing.

1079
00:44:35,751 --> 00:44:37,584
Brilliant, Dubey.

1080
00:44:37,709 --> 00:44:40,583
Sir, I'm spending
without holding back.

1081
00:44:40,584 --> 00:44:42,125
Good. Spend as much as needed.

1082
00:44:42,126 --> 00:44:44,126
There shouldn't be any shortage of money.
Understood, Dubey?

1083
00:44:44,251 --> 00:44:47,709
- Here. Take it. Happy now.
- Thank you, sir.

1084
00:44:47,834 --> 00:44:50,625
<i>[singing] Kashi rocks, Patna rocks,</i>

1085
00:44:50,626 --> 00:44:52,292
Shut up, you idiots!
Let me rest.

1086
00:44:52,293 --> 00:44:54,792
Give me a massage.
<i>[group singing] the whole city rocks...</i>

1087
00:44:54,793 --> 00:44:55,792
[gunfire]

1088
00:44:55,793 --> 00:44:57,001
Shut up!

1089
00:44:57,168 --> 00:44:58,792
[soft music]

1090
00:44:58,793 --> 00:45:01,168
Hey, idiot!
Here's 3200.

1091
00:45:01,418 --> 00:45:03,584
Keep the camera on me.
I'm going to do a stunt.

1092
00:45:04,626 --> 00:45:05,459
That's…

1093
00:45:05,668 --> 00:45:07,625
All right.
But who are you, mister?

1094
00:45:07,626 --> 00:45:09,168
Start sound. Cameras.

1095
00:45:09,293 --> 00:45:11,501
- Rolling... maybe.
- Action!

1096
00:45:11,626 --> 00:45:14,376
[upbeat music]
[gunfire]

1097
00:45:16,459 --> 00:45:18,543
[helicopter whirring]

1098
00:45:22,626 --> 00:45:24,458
Mind-blowing. Fantabulous.

1099
00:45:24,459 --> 00:45:26,209
- Hey, Director!
- Yes, Anna.

1100
00:45:26,376 --> 00:45:27,418
What's mind-blowing?

1101
00:45:28,418 --> 00:45:30,834
I want to do what that loser did.

1102
00:45:32,626 --> 00:45:33,918
You mean the stunt.

1103
00:45:34,043 --> 00:45:36,084
Stunt or whatever,
I want to do it.

1104
00:45:37,043 --> 00:45:38,043
Ready?

1105
00:45:38,293 --> 00:45:39,417
Action!

1106
00:45:39,418 --> 00:45:41,543
[upbeat music]

1107
00:45:41,751 --> 00:45:44,750
Director. Director.
I don't want to do action.

1108
00:45:44,751 --> 00:45:46,917
Get me down, I have vertigo.

1109
00:45:46,918 --> 00:45:48,334
Say cut, director.

1110
00:45:48,501 --> 00:45:50,000
Why is he screaming?

1111
00:45:50,001 --> 00:45:51,000
You know?

1112
00:45:51,001 --> 00:45:52,375
You wouldn't be screaming at all.

1113
00:45:52,376 --> 00:45:53,292
Why?

1114
00:45:53,293 --> 00:45:55,125
The chopper would never
have taken off with you.

1115
00:45:55,126 --> 00:45:56,543
[laughter]

1116
00:45:56,709 --> 00:45:58,584
- Get me down. I have vertigo.
- What is this?

1117
00:45:58,709 --> 00:46:00,543
He's ruined the whole shot.

1118
00:46:00,834 --> 00:46:02,376
Why do you hire people like him?

1119
00:46:02,668 --> 00:46:04,251
- [laughter]
- I have vertigo. I have vertigo.

1120
00:46:04,376 --> 00:46:05,917
That's his job, Anna.

1121
00:46:05,918 --> 00:46:07,417
It's not your job to hang like this.

1122
00:46:07,418 --> 00:46:10,125
You've left me hanging,
Ramprasad Udyavar.

1123
00:46:10,126 --> 00:46:12,708
I started such an expensive film
on your advice.

1124
00:46:12,709 --> 00:46:13,543
Look, Sinha.

1125
00:46:13,668 --> 00:46:14,793
I told you before.

1126
00:46:15,084 --> 00:46:17,793
If the opposition comes to power,
I can't help you.

1127
00:46:17,959 --> 00:46:18,917
Bye.

1128
00:46:18,918 --> 00:46:21,543
- [phone beeping]
- Hello. Hello. Hello.

1129
00:46:21,959 --> 00:46:23,667
- Hello.
- [intense music]

1130
00:46:23,668 --> 00:46:24,418
Hello?

1131
00:46:24,543 --> 00:46:26,792
Mr. Sinha, it's an IT raid.

1132
00:46:26,793 --> 00:46:28,375
[dramatic music]

1133
00:46:28,376 --> 00:46:30,334
Calm down, Mr. Sinha. Calm down.

1134
00:46:30,918 --> 00:46:34,375
No calm, sir!
I'm bringing a revolution.

1135
00:46:34,376 --> 00:46:36,043
Boom. Boom. Boom.

1136
00:46:36,209 --> 00:46:38,501
I've planted explosives everywhere.

1137
00:46:38,626 --> 00:46:41,583
Just give me the signal
on that tower.

1138
00:46:41,584 --> 00:46:42,459
What's he saying?

1139
00:46:42,668 --> 00:46:44,792
He's saying there's
a detonator up there.

1140
00:46:44,793 --> 00:46:47,834
As soon as it's pressed,
there'll be a small 100-gram blast.

1141
00:46:48,543 --> 00:46:51,833
After that, he's loaded it
with 750 kilos of explosives.

1142
00:46:51,834 --> 00:46:53,751
- he'll blow everyone up. Right?
- Yes.

1143
00:46:53,876 --> 00:46:54,793
[laughing loudly]

1144
00:46:54,918 --> 00:46:56,459
[silence]

1145
00:46:57,543 --> 00:46:58,376
Hey?

1146
00:46:58,709 --> 00:47:01,667
He's saying budget is not an issue.
Blow it up.

1147
00:47:01,668 --> 00:47:02,875
Hallelujah. Hallelujah.

1148
00:47:02,876 --> 00:47:03,918
Come on, clear the ground.

1149
00:47:04,043 --> 00:47:05,834
Let me set the shot.
Full lights.

1150
00:47:06,418 --> 00:47:07,792
It's daylight!

1151
00:47:07,793 --> 00:47:09,292
[comic music]

1152
00:47:09,293 --> 00:47:12,168
We'll shoot the climax here.

1153
00:47:12,626 --> 00:47:14,543
Rajeev, this is your death scene.

1154
00:47:14,709 --> 00:47:16,876
You get shot, and your chapter ends.

1155
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:18,459
Good riddance.

1156
00:47:18,584 --> 00:47:20,084
The moment you're shot,

1157
00:47:20,418 --> 00:47:25,376
you close your eyes and die.

1158
00:47:25,543 --> 00:47:27,668
As soon as you close your eyes,

1159
00:47:28,209 --> 00:47:31,583
Nadia and Anna will embrace each
other in a tight hug in happiness.

1160
00:47:31,584 --> 00:47:32,543
Too much happily.

1161
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:35,000
Nice. Nice.

1162
00:47:35,001 --> 00:47:36,000
[laugh]

1163
00:47:36,001 --> 00:47:39,043
[emotional music]

1164
00:47:39,334 --> 00:47:41,000
I guess Dev-Das won't stop
till they turn you…

1165
00:47:41,001 --> 00:47:43,084
into Amitabh Bachchan of action films.

1166
00:47:43,626 --> 00:47:44,542
Yes.

1167
00:47:44,543 --> 00:47:45,833
[soft music playing]

1168
00:47:45,834 --> 00:47:47,959
But this Amitabh Bachchan
just won't die.

1169
00:47:48,584 --> 00:47:49,793
- What?
- Ready?

1170
00:47:50,043 --> 00:47:52,501
- Start sound. Cameras.
- Rolling.

1171
00:47:52,751 --> 00:47:54,668
[playful music]

1172
00:47:55,168 --> 00:47:56,043
Action!

1173
00:47:56,251 --> 00:47:58,543
- [gunfire]
- [groans in pain]

1174
00:48:01,418 --> 00:48:05,209
[intense music]

1175
00:48:06,251 --> 00:48:07,043
Fire.

1176
00:48:08,334 --> 00:48:11,168
[groaning]

1177
00:48:12,501 --> 00:48:13,584
[gasps]

1178
00:48:14,543 --> 00:48:16,543
[groaning]

1179
00:48:16,834 --> 00:48:18,167
Baljeet!

1180
00:48:18,168 --> 00:48:20,084
- No!
- Oh, God.

1181
00:48:20,584 --> 00:48:22,584
[emotional music]

1182
00:48:26,293 --> 00:48:28,293
[emotional music continues]

1183
00:48:30,334 --> 00:48:32,459
[screams]

1184
00:48:36,418 --> 00:48:37,918
[comic music]

1185
00:48:39,709 --> 00:48:40,708
Why isn't he dying?

1186
00:48:40,709 --> 00:48:41,918
What is this?

1187
00:48:43,001 --> 00:48:44,792
Hey, Shoot him again. Twice.

1188
00:48:44,793 --> 00:48:45,584
Okay.

1189
00:48:45,876 --> 00:48:47,876
- [gunfire]
- [groans in pain]

1190
00:48:49,959 --> 00:48:51,543
[intense music]

1191
00:48:52,251 --> 00:48:53,126
[gasps]

1192
00:48:53,543 --> 00:48:55,084
- [emotional music]
- He's dead.

1193
00:48:59,543 --> 00:49:01,543
[screams]

1194
00:49:02,209 --> 00:49:03,584
Just die.

1195
00:49:03,834 --> 00:49:04,708
Die.

1196
00:49:04,709 --> 00:49:06,418
Are they shooting him with bullets
or vitamins?

1197
00:49:06,543 --> 00:49:07,500
He keeps getting up.

1198
00:49:07,501 --> 00:49:08,834
He just won't die.

1199
00:49:09,001 --> 00:49:10,584
He's not going to die.

1200
00:49:11,918 --> 00:49:13,626
He knows what happens if he dies.

1201
00:49:13,793 --> 00:49:15,459
I'll kill him.

1202
00:49:17,251 --> 00:49:19,251
- [gunfire]
- [groans in pain]

1203
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:23,834
[intense music]

1204
00:49:26,668 --> 00:49:28,168
[rapid gunfire]

1205
00:49:30,084 --> 00:49:31,583
Just die already!

1206
00:49:31,584 --> 00:49:32,709
Dev-Das!

1207
00:49:33,293 --> 00:49:34,543
Coming, Romeo, coming.

1208
00:49:34,668 --> 00:49:36,583
- [rapid gunfire]
- [groaning]

1209
00:49:36,584 --> 00:49:38,043
Why won't you die?

1210
00:49:38,168 --> 00:49:39,626
I'm putting some soul into dying.

1211
00:49:39,751 --> 00:49:41,417
Who puts soul into dying?

1212
00:49:41,418 --> 00:49:43,834
Oh God, these actors are at it again.

1213
00:49:44,084 --> 00:49:46,250
Dev-Das, what did you say he was?

1214
00:49:46,251 --> 00:49:48,334
A dog!
But he's a damn cat!

1215
00:49:48,459 --> 00:49:50,958
We knock him down nine times,
he still won't die.

1216
00:49:50,959 --> 00:49:52,334
Turn off the camera, come on.

1217
00:49:52,459 --> 00:49:54,709
Just use real bullets and die!

1218
00:49:55,251 --> 00:49:56,126
What?

1219
00:49:56,793 --> 00:49:59,251
Bloody goldfish, you want to shoot me!

1220
00:49:59,418 --> 00:50:00,668
Let me go.

1221
00:50:01,209 --> 00:50:02,459
I'll shoot you.

1222
00:50:03,959 --> 00:50:05,209
Have you lost your mind?

1223
00:50:05,334 --> 00:50:06,958
Have you lost it?

1224
00:50:06,959 --> 00:50:08,625
[explosion]

1225
00:50:08,626 --> 00:50:10,168
Okay, done blast.

1226
00:50:10,334 --> 00:50:11,293
Hallelujah.

1227
00:50:11,459 --> 00:50:12,417
Das! Das!

1228
00:50:12,418 --> 00:50:15,959
Tell Dominic not to trigger the blast.

1229
00:50:16,334 --> 00:50:18,958
Dominic... blast...

1230
00:50:18,959 --> 00:50:20,543
[silence]

1231
00:50:20,793 --> 00:50:22,917
Signal received. Okay.

1232
00:50:22,918 --> 00:50:25,418
[suspenseful music]

1233
00:50:25,584 --> 00:50:27,417
Stop it!

1234
00:50:27,418 --> 00:50:28,667
[electrical buzzing]

1235
00:50:28,668 --> 00:50:29,376
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

1236
00:50:29,501 --> 00:50:31,084
- <i>♪ To the jungle welcome ♪</i>
- [explosions]

1237
00:50:31,209 --> 00:50:32,084
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

1238
00:50:32,251 --> 00:50:33,875
<i>♪ Everyone, come welcome ♪</i>

1239
00:50:33,876 --> 00:50:34,708
<i>♪ Welcome ♪</i>

1240
00:50:34,709 --> 00:50:36,668
<i>♪ To the party, come welcome ♪</i>

1241
00:50:36,793 --> 00:50:38,918
- Give me the phone...
- At least...

1242
00:50:39,084 --> 00:50:42,501
[Welcome theme playing]

1243
00:50:45,668 --> 00:50:47,084
Diwali!

1244
00:50:47,876 --> 00:50:50,668
[explosion continues]

1245
00:50:51,293 --> 00:50:52,793
Why am I panicking?

1246
00:50:53,334 --> 00:50:54,959
We were supposed to blow it up.

1247
00:50:55,876 --> 00:50:56,834
But that's...

1248
00:50:58,584 --> 00:51:00,083
- Excuse me!
- Yes?

1249
00:51:00,084 --> 00:51:01,584
- That carpet too.
- Yes.

1250
00:51:03,126 --> 00:51:04,793
Du... Du... Dubey.

1251
00:51:04,918 --> 00:51:06,584
My secret phone.

1252
00:51:06,709 --> 00:51:07,708
Dubey.

1253
00:51:07,709 --> 00:51:10,293
[phone ringing]

1254
00:51:10,459 --> 00:51:11,333
Who is this?

1255
00:51:11,334 --> 00:51:12,500
It's me. Sinha.

1256
00:51:12,501 --> 00:51:14,500
Sir. Good news.

1257
00:51:14,501 --> 00:51:15,500
[laughing loudly]

1258
00:51:15,501 --> 00:51:17,000
That 142 crores set we were
supposed to blow up...

1259
00:51:17,001 --> 00:51:18,083
you didn't blow it up?

1260
00:51:18,084 --> 00:51:19,167
Why wouldn't I?

1261
00:51:19,168 --> 00:51:20,208
That's exactly why I'm here.

1262
00:51:20,209 --> 00:51:22,209
It's gone, sir. In pieces.

1263
00:51:23,459 --> 00:51:25,876
And do you know what's bonus?

1264
00:51:26,043 --> 00:51:26,876
What?

1265
00:51:27,084 --> 00:51:28,959
The camera wasn't on.

1266
00:51:29,209 --> 00:51:31,543
You weren't supposed to blow it up.

1267
00:51:31,876 --> 00:51:32,334
Why?

1268
00:51:32,459 --> 00:51:35,376
The income tax raided me, Dubey.

1269
00:51:35,543 --> 00:51:38,333
From the carpet to my pants,
they took everything.

1270
00:51:38,334 --> 00:51:39,584
What do we do now?

1271
00:51:39,751 --> 00:51:42,958
Finish this film in one day.

1272
00:51:42,959 --> 00:51:45,583
We've only got one way to make money.

1273
00:51:45,584 --> 00:51:48,042
Make me a hit film.

1274
00:51:48,043 --> 00:51:50,042
Or I'll shoot everyone.

1275
00:51:50,043 --> 00:51:51,250
[gunshot]

1276
00:51:51,251 --> 00:51:55,209
Beg them to complete the film.

1277
00:51:55,334 --> 00:51:57,334
[gibberish sound]

1278
00:52:00,168 --> 00:52:03,334
[gibberish sound continues]

1279
00:52:03,543 --> 00:52:05,167
Now what can I do?

1280
00:52:05,168 --> 00:52:06,834
Isn't Dubey sounding absurd?

1281
00:52:06,959 --> 00:52:08,833
How will we finish shooting
in one day?

1282
00:52:08,834 --> 00:52:09,917
It's all his fault.

1283
00:52:09,918 --> 00:52:12,583
Yes. I kept telling him not
to blow it up.

1284
00:52:12,584 --> 00:52:13,917
But he didn't listen.

1285
00:52:13,918 --> 00:52:15,833
You didn't say anything.

1286
00:52:15,834 --> 00:52:17,418
I was signalling you...
don't blow it up.

1287
00:52:17,543 --> 00:52:19,500
- What did you do?
- Think about what we do next?

1288
00:52:19,501 --> 00:52:20,375
And how will we do it?

1289
00:52:20,376 --> 00:52:23,000
We don't have a set
or a location or money.

1290
00:52:23,001 --> 00:52:23,792
How do we do it?

1291
00:52:23,793 --> 00:52:24,917
I know about a location.

1292
00:52:24,918 --> 00:52:26,376
It's 20 kilometres from the border.

1293
00:52:26,584 --> 00:52:27,584
Azadganj

1294
00:52:27,793 --> 00:52:30,458
That village matches
exactly with your set.

1295
00:52:30,459 --> 00:52:32,042
It can be of use to you.

1296
00:52:32,043 --> 00:52:34,543
But... let me warn you.

1297
00:52:35,001 --> 00:52:36,083
There is a problem.

1298
00:52:36,084 --> 00:52:38,251
- Will the location cost money?
- Free. It's free.

1299
00:52:38,376 --> 00:52:39,542
Will we need permission?

1300
00:52:39,543 --> 00:52:41,583
Why need permission when it's free?

1301
00:52:41,584 --> 00:52:42,834
Then what is the problem?

1302
00:52:42,959 --> 00:52:45,043
Some villagers live
in the village.

1303
00:52:45,418 --> 00:52:46,876
Villagers in the village?

1304
00:52:47,168 --> 00:52:48,293
No...

1305
00:52:48,418 --> 00:52:51,001
We'll use the villagers as background.

1306
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:54,709
Yes, we won't tell the actors
they are villagers,

1307
00:52:54,834 --> 00:52:56,042
Otherwise, they won't cooperate.

1308
00:52:56,043 --> 00:52:56,708
No, no.

1309
00:52:56,709 --> 00:52:57,833
And don't worry about the shoot.

1310
00:52:57,834 --> 00:52:59,917
I will put up cameras
all over the village.

1311
00:52:59,918 --> 00:53:01,208
We'll finish shooting in a single day.

1312
00:53:01,209 --> 00:53:03,418
- There is another problem.
- What?

1313
00:53:03,626 --> 00:53:05,542
There is no road to this village?

1314
00:53:05,543 --> 00:53:07,834
Do the villagers fly to their village?

1315
00:53:08,126 --> 00:53:09,583
What are you talking about?

1316
00:53:09,584 --> 00:53:11,084
I have three helicopters on standby.

1317
00:53:11,251 --> 00:53:13,376
They have been paid
in full for both ways.

1318
00:53:13,543 --> 00:53:14,667
They will have to bring us back.

1319
00:53:14,668 --> 00:53:15,583
There is a problem.

1320
00:53:15,584 --> 00:53:16,833
What are you talking about?

1321
00:53:16,834 --> 00:53:18,625
Location is not a problem.
We don't need permission.

1322
00:53:18,626 --> 00:53:19,583
There are villagers in the village.

1323
00:53:19,584 --> 00:53:20,542
We have helicopters!

1324
00:53:20,543 --> 00:53:21,500
What problem do you have?

1325
00:53:21,501 --> 00:53:22,917
[silence]

1326
00:53:22,918 --> 00:53:25,376
What is the problem?
Why did you blow it up?

1327
00:53:26,668 --> 00:53:28,709
You guys didn't hear
the main problem.

1328
00:53:29,334 --> 00:53:31,834
The main problem... Hallelujah.

1329
00:53:32,043 --> 00:53:33,918
Hey... brother.

1330
00:53:34,459 --> 00:53:35,709
How is this even possible?

1331
00:53:35,918 --> 00:53:37,501
Do you have a brain or bullshit?

1332
00:53:37,668 --> 00:53:39,501
How can we finish shooting
in a single day?

1333
00:53:39,668 --> 00:53:40,501
Hey, Pen drive.

1334
00:53:40,918 --> 00:53:41,834
Yes, bro.

1335
00:53:42,001 --> 00:53:43,584
Are you making a film
or instant noodles?

1336
00:53:43,709 --> 00:53:45,334
Finish shooting in a day?

1337
00:53:45,584 --> 00:53:47,834
He's not ready to die in the film,

1338
00:53:47,959 --> 00:53:49,458
and you are screwing with the film.

1339
00:53:49,459 --> 00:53:51,417
You said you'll give me that.

1340
00:53:51,418 --> 00:53:51,959
What?

1341
00:53:52,084 --> 00:53:54,333
That thing that heroes get in the film.

1342
00:53:54,334 --> 00:53:55,000
Heroine?

1343
00:53:55,001 --> 00:53:56,083
Did you promise him that?

1344
00:53:56,084 --> 00:53:57,334
What are you saying, Anna?

1345
00:53:57,501 --> 00:53:58,750
This is a family film.

1346
00:53:58,751 --> 00:54:01,376
Not at all... I never said that.

1347
00:54:01,501 --> 00:54:02,626
Hold on.

1348
00:54:02,876 --> 00:54:04,668
Brother will do no such thing.

1349
00:54:05,084 --> 00:54:06,459
I am ready to do it.

1350
00:54:06,626 --> 00:54:08,042
One day, brother?

1351
00:54:08,043 --> 00:54:09,543
Let's end this chapter in one day.

1352
00:54:10,834 --> 00:54:12,125
I cannot tolerate this anymore.

1353
00:54:12,126 --> 00:54:14,126
[awkward music]

1354
00:54:14,751 --> 00:54:16,584
I cannot see them
hugging each other.

1355
00:54:18,084 --> 00:54:20,084
[awkward music]

1356
00:54:19,668 --> 00:54:20,668
I am ready.

1357
00:54:21,376 --> 00:54:22,918
I don't want to see their faces.

1358
00:54:23,084 --> 00:54:24,834
But your face was priceless

1359
00:54:25,376 --> 00:54:27,959
when she was with me.

1360
00:54:28,084 --> 00:54:29,792
[naughty sound]

1361
00:54:29,793 --> 00:54:32,042
I really wanna mop
the floor with you two.

1362
00:54:32,043 --> 00:54:32,875
Listen, Mrs. Doubtfire.

1363
00:54:32,876 --> 00:54:34,626
If you like mopping so much,
mop the floor.

1364
00:54:34,751 --> 00:54:35,750
The floor is pretty dirty.

1365
00:54:35,751 --> 00:54:37,667
Even your face is pretty dirty.

1366
00:54:37,668 --> 00:54:38,793
Do you want me to mop that?

1367
00:54:38,918 --> 00:54:39,833
- Hey...
- Calm down.

1368
00:54:39,834 --> 00:54:40,542
Calm down, guys.

1369
00:54:40,543 --> 00:54:42,042
- Wait a minute.
- Why do you keep fighting over everything?

1370
00:54:42,043 --> 00:54:44,083
Shut up! Hopping like a frog.

1371
00:54:44,084 --> 00:54:45,833
Don't call a rhinoceros a frog.

1372
00:54:45,834 --> 00:54:46,793
Just stop it.

1373
00:54:46,918 --> 00:54:48,084
You go fish.

1374
00:54:48,251 --> 00:54:49,500
Go to hell all of you.

1375
00:54:49,501 --> 00:54:51,793
We have no interest
in going to your home.

1376
00:54:52,084 --> 00:54:53,168
Stop it.

1377
00:54:53,293 --> 00:54:54,418
Why you...

1378
00:54:55,209 --> 00:54:56,875
- What are you doing?
- What did you do, idiot?

1379
00:54:56,876 --> 00:54:57,834
What is this?

1380
00:54:58,501 --> 00:55:00,167
[screams]

1381
00:55:00,168 --> 00:55:03,417
- It's not acid. It's water.
- Stop overacting! It's water

1382
00:55:03,418 --> 00:55:04,333
Why you...

1383
00:55:04,334 --> 00:55:05,876
Beat him. Beat him.

1384
00:55:06,001 --> 00:55:07,125
What are you guys doing?

1385
00:55:07,126 --> 00:55:08,751
Stop them, Anna.

1386
00:55:08,918 --> 00:55:10,168
Today is my rest day.

1387
00:55:11,001 --> 00:55:12,167
Calm Down.

1388
00:55:12,168 --> 00:55:13,833
If you guys keep fighting this way,

1389
00:55:13,834 --> 00:55:16,418
the film will never get completed
nor will anyone get paid.

1390
00:55:17,834 --> 00:55:19,793
- No lying down, sit down.
- Yes.

1391
00:55:22,251 --> 00:55:24,001
Stop blabbering!

1392
00:55:24,501 --> 00:55:26,668
The set blew up because of you guys.

1393
00:55:26,793 --> 00:55:28,292
Sinha sir has clearly said,

1394
00:55:28,293 --> 00:55:30,000
if the film doesn't get completed
in two days,

1395
00:55:30,001 --> 00:55:31,626
no one gets the final payment.

1396
00:55:31,918 --> 00:55:34,167
We'll leave for the shoot tomorrow

1397
00:55:34,168 --> 00:55:35,709
and go to a real location.

1398
00:55:35,834 --> 00:55:38,459
That location is
very similar to our set.

1399
00:55:38,584 --> 00:55:41,501
Yes. And the cameras will be all over.

1400
00:55:41,668 --> 00:55:43,417
Like in Bigg Boss house.

1401
00:55:43,418 --> 00:55:44,626
We'll finish shooting in a single day.

1402
00:55:44,793 --> 00:55:49,043
There you will meet some talented
actors with a theatre background.

1403
00:55:49,251 --> 00:55:53,584
And you all have
to improvise with them.

1404
00:55:53,793 --> 00:55:56,751
We'll be there with you in uniform.

1405
00:55:56,918 --> 00:55:58,417
Since he'll be holding the camera,

1406
00:55:58,418 --> 00:55:59,668
he can pan on anyone at any time.

1407
00:55:59,793 --> 00:56:02,208
And according to production,

1408
00:56:02,209 --> 00:56:04,501
no assistant, no vanity van,
no makeup.

1409
00:56:04,709 --> 00:56:06,043
And most importantly...

1410
00:56:06,418 --> 00:56:08,709
[silence]

1411
00:56:10,168 --> 00:56:12,459
- Did he say something?
- I didn't understand.

1412
00:56:12,959 --> 00:56:14,168
- Correct.
- Understood?

1413
00:56:14,334 --> 00:56:17,668
He's saying everyone
should be ready at 7 am.

1414
00:56:17,834 --> 00:56:19,083
The helicopter will be there.

1415
00:56:19,084 --> 00:56:20,626
- Correct?
- That's what I said.

1416
00:56:20,918 --> 00:56:23,876
<i>♪ Welcome welcome welcome ♪</i>

1417
00:56:25,334 --> 00:56:28,251
[birds chirping]

1418
00:56:28,584 --> 00:56:31,043
Dominic... why the long face?

1419
00:56:31,334 --> 00:56:32,709
Everything is set now.

1420
00:56:32,834 --> 00:56:34,333
You guys didn't listen to me.

1421
00:56:34,334 --> 00:56:37,250
If we didn't listen to you,
then how are we here with the works?

1422
00:56:37,251 --> 00:56:39,583
I mean... you didn't hear me
out completely.

1423
00:56:39,584 --> 00:56:41,084
Fine, we didn't listen. Tell us now.

1424
00:56:41,209 --> 00:56:44,043
What I'm going to say now is bad.

1425
00:56:44,168 --> 00:56:46,375
Whether it's bad or not,
just tell us.

1426
00:56:46,376 --> 00:56:49,000
It's both. It's bad
and it's the whole truth.

1427
00:56:49,001 --> 00:56:51,083
The village I told you about

1428
00:56:51,084 --> 00:56:53,083
is often raided by mujahideen.

1429
00:56:53,084 --> 00:56:55,626
[ominous music]

1430
00:56:55,876 --> 00:56:58,084
Mujahideen? Alauddin's brother?

1431
00:56:58,459 --> 00:57:00,083
No, man.

1432
00:57:00,084 --> 00:57:02,251
Mujahideen terrorists.

1433
00:57:02,626 --> 00:57:05,626
[horses galloping]

1434
00:57:06,043 --> 00:57:07,293
Dacoits.

1435
00:57:07,459 --> 00:57:09,084
Yes terrorists!

1436
00:57:09,251 --> 00:57:11,918
His name is Zatara!

1437
00:57:13,001 --> 00:57:15,584
[suspenseful music]

1438
00:57:18,876 --> 00:57:21,626
[horses galloping]

1439
00:57:23,084 --> 00:57:24,251
Hey man,

1440
00:57:24,418 --> 00:57:26,625
I've decided not to go with you.

1441
00:57:26,626 --> 00:57:28,084
The helicopter's going to drop you

1442
00:57:28,251 --> 00:57:30,000
and pick you up at 5:30 pm.

1443
00:57:30,001 --> 00:57:31,584
Bye. Hallelujah.

1444
00:57:33,668 --> 00:57:35,751
It's okay. They don't come often.

1445
00:57:35,876 --> 00:57:39,876
Right. They must be
those small-time radicals.

1446
00:57:42,626 --> 00:57:46,293
[suspenseful music]

1447
00:57:48,793 --> 00:57:50,375
We are not that unlucky

1448
00:57:50,376 --> 00:57:52,333
that they will show up
when we arrive.

1449
00:57:52,334 --> 00:57:53,376
- They show up rarely.
- Exactly.

1450
00:57:54,418 --> 00:57:56,417
[tense music]

1451
00:57:56,418 --> 00:57:57,918
Run!

1452
00:57:58,459 --> 00:58:02,584
- [horses neighing]
- [people screaming]

1453
00:58:07,251 --> 00:58:09,168
Run! They're here!

1454
00:58:10,334 --> 00:58:12,334
[horses neighing]

1455
00:58:21,084 --> 00:58:23,834
And that cross-eyed Dominic made it
sound like it's an entire army.

1456
00:58:23,959 --> 00:58:24,958
To hell with them!

1457
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:26,959
[mysterious music]

1458
00:58:29,876 --> 00:58:31,876
[mysterious music continues]

1459
00:58:32,459 --> 00:58:33,334
Villagers!

1460
00:58:35,084 --> 00:58:36,834
Remember, Zatara personally told

1461
00:58:37,543 --> 00:58:39,209
you not to touch that well.

1462
00:58:39,334 --> 00:58:41,918
And he tried to drink from that well.

1463
00:58:43,334 --> 00:58:45,334
[groaning]

1464
00:58:46,376 --> 00:58:48,376
[door opens]

1465
00:58:49,709 --> 00:58:51,709
[ominous music]

1466
00:58:56,168 --> 00:58:58,168
[ominous music continues]

1467
00:59:07,209 --> 00:59:08,251
Rascals!

1468
00:59:09,793 --> 00:59:11,834
You two belong to our village.

1469
00:59:12,418 --> 00:59:13,626
You joined hands with them.

1470
00:59:14,918 --> 00:59:16,084
[spits]

1471
00:59:20,293 --> 00:59:21,334
[spits]

1472
00:59:23,084 --> 00:59:25,626
This attitude of yours... makes Zatara

1473
00:59:26,584 --> 00:59:28,209
- [kisses]
- crazy about you.

1474
00:59:29,668 --> 00:59:31,668
[mysterious music]

1475
00:59:38,668 --> 00:59:41,626
Zatara! Set Azadganj free!

1476
00:59:43,668 --> 00:59:45,084
- [everyone shouting]
- Father!

1477
00:59:47,209 --> 00:59:49,293
Dad. Dad...

1478
00:59:51,168 --> 00:59:54,084
Neither Azadganj, nor Zoya...

1479
00:59:54,209 --> 00:59:57,418
Zatara share them with anyone.

1480
00:59:57,543 --> 01:00:00,959
Anyone who interferes
will be reduced to dust.

1481
01:00:01,334 --> 01:00:03,334
[mysterious music]

1482
01:00:05,459 --> 01:00:09,084
The day will come
when you'll be reduced to dust.

1483
01:00:12,459 --> 01:00:16,168
The day will come
when you will accept Zatara's love.

1484
01:00:19,168 --> 01:00:21,376
Your obsession will never come true.

1485
01:00:22,668 --> 01:00:24,668
[ominous music]

1486
01:00:28,959 --> 01:00:34,001
All of you pray
that the Indian government

1487
01:00:34,668 --> 01:00:36,626
gives in to our demands by 5:30 pm.

1488
01:00:37,084 --> 01:00:39,168
If I see any activity
in this village before that,

1489
01:00:39,959 --> 01:00:41,668
then no one will be spared.

1490
01:00:42,626 --> 01:00:45,001
[gibberish]

1491
01:00:48,709 --> 01:00:50,918
[gibberish continues]

1492
01:00:52,001 --> 01:00:53,543
What is the old woman saying?

1493
01:00:53,751 --> 01:00:54,834
One minute.

1494
01:00:55,043 --> 01:00:56,168
Old woman...

1495
01:00:57,626 --> 01:00:59,376
either you speak, or you cry.

1496
01:00:59,709 --> 01:01:01,042
[awkward music]

1497
01:01:01,043 --> 01:01:02,418
Auntie is absolutely right.

1498
01:01:03,459 --> 01:01:05,459
[comic music]

1499
01:01:05,834 --> 01:01:07,209
How did he understand him?

1500
01:01:08,751 --> 01:01:10,251
Old man...

1501
01:01:10,418 --> 01:01:12,793
you think you understand her?

1502
01:01:12,918 --> 01:01:15,084
[arabic language]

1503
01:01:16,251 --> 01:01:17,709
[arabic language]

1504
01:01:18,001 --> 01:01:20,209
[arabic language]

1505
01:01:20,501 --> 01:01:21,417
What?

1506
01:01:21,418 --> 01:01:23,043
Better face the reality.

1507
01:01:24,209 --> 01:01:25,834
They both are crazy?

1508
01:01:25,959 --> 01:01:27,084
You're right, brother.

1509
01:01:27,251 --> 01:01:29,209
- Let's go.
- [horse neighs]

1510
01:01:32,751 --> 01:01:36,626
Lord... is there anyone
who can free us from this captivity?

1511
01:01:36,793 --> 01:01:38,793
[suspenseful music]

1512
01:01:42,084 --> 01:01:46,251
Send someone to free us
from Zatara's wrath.

1513
01:01:46,501 --> 01:01:48,501
[suspenseful music continues]

1514
01:01:49,043 --> 01:01:50,250
Ready.

1515
01:01:50,251 --> 01:01:51,042
Camera.

1516
01:01:51,043 --> 01:01:52,293
- Rolling.
- Yes.

1517
01:01:52,668 --> 01:01:54,626
Show us their faces.

1518
01:01:56,459 --> 01:01:58,459
- [playful music]
- [kisses]

1519
01:01:59,626 --> 01:02:02,834
[gibberish]

1520
01:02:03,834 --> 01:02:07,334
[helicopter whirring]

1521
01:02:10,709 --> 01:02:14,334
Those who will be our armour...
and our arsenal.

1522
01:02:14,834 --> 01:02:17,001
Bend over, fatso. Bend down.

1523
01:02:17,168 --> 01:02:18,084
Climb up.

1524
01:02:18,959 --> 01:02:19,958
[groans]

1525
01:02:19,959 --> 01:02:21,293
- Bye, guys.
- See you soon.

1526
01:02:22,126 --> 01:02:24,126
[helicopter whirring]

1527
01:02:26,001 --> 01:02:28,293
Shower your grace from the skies.

1528
01:02:29,793 --> 01:02:32,584
- [helicopter whirring]
- [cheering]

1529
01:02:35,668 --> 01:02:36,668
Let's go.

1530
01:02:38,959 --> 01:02:40,959
[helicopter whirring]

1531
01:02:45,793 --> 01:02:47,793
[helicopter whirring continues]

1532
01:02:58,251 --> 01:03:00,251
[comic music]

1533
01:03:01,168 --> 01:03:02,293
Why did you push me?

1534
01:03:02,418 --> 01:03:04,751
I didn't push you, I kicked you.

1535
01:03:04,918 --> 01:03:05,834
Yes!

1536
01:03:06,168 --> 01:03:07,168
Help me.

1537
01:03:08,001 --> 01:03:09,084
What are you doing?

1538
01:03:10,043 --> 01:03:11,543
Come on, baby.

1539
01:03:13,168 --> 01:03:14,292
Help me.

1540
01:03:14,293 --> 01:03:16,918
Hey... she won't go with you.

1541
01:03:17,084 --> 01:03:18,084
Get lost.

1542
01:03:18,376 --> 01:03:19,418
Rajeev.

1543
01:03:20,043 --> 01:03:21,500
Help me also.

1544
01:03:21,501 --> 01:03:24,751
Let's go, horsey. Come on.

1545
01:03:27,918 --> 01:03:29,918
[bird cawing]

1546
01:03:30,293 --> 01:03:31,708
Listen carefully, guys.

1547
01:03:31,709 --> 01:03:33,834
We have installed cameras everywhere.

1548
01:03:33,959 --> 01:03:35,834
We'll say action now

1549
01:03:36,001 --> 01:03:38,875
and cut directly at 5:30 pm.

1550
01:03:38,876 --> 01:03:40,668
- Right.
- This is called guerrilla shooting.

1551
01:03:40,876 --> 01:03:42,083
What is it called?

1552
01:03:42,084 --> 01:03:43,042
Guerilla shooting!

1553
01:03:43,043 --> 01:03:44,083
What is it called?

1554
01:03:44,084 --> 01:03:45,626
[All] Guerilla shooting!

1555
01:03:46,459 --> 01:03:48,459
- [woman gasps]
- [gorilla growls]

1556
01:03:50,751 --> 01:03:51,834
Gorilla sound?

1557
01:03:52,376 --> 01:03:53,709
Gorilla!

1558
01:03:54,043 --> 01:03:55,250
Indian army!

1559
01:03:55,251 --> 01:03:57,001
- What?
- Show me.

1560
01:03:57,584 --> 01:04:00,209
[suspenseful music]

1561
01:04:00,501 --> 01:04:02,793
The Indian Army
in Azadganj for the first time.

1562
01:04:03,376 --> 01:04:04,834
And we're feasting on fruits.

1563
01:04:05,293 --> 01:04:06,209
Here you go.

1564
01:04:07,959 --> 01:04:09,251
Go on, Abdullah.

1565
01:04:09,501 --> 01:04:11,084
We're guarding the Sector 14 mines.

1566
01:04:11,251 --> 01:04:13,334
And the update is
that the Indian army is here.

1567
01:04:13,709 --> 01:04:16,376
<i>If you can, please check
from your binoculars.</i>

1568
01:04:17,293 --> 01:04:18,708
[gasp]

1569
01:04:18,709 --> 01:04:20,251
- Indian army?
- Yes.

1570
01:04:20,418 --> 01:04:23,084
I think my binoculars are busted.

1571
01:04:23,293 --> 01:04:25,043
The Indian army is not in range.

1572
01:04:25,209 --> 01:04:27,084
But I can see you two.

1573
01:04:28,084 --> 01:04:30,209
And we can see them, sir.

1574
01:04:30,334 --> 01:04:31,334
How many?

1575
01:04:32,001 --> 01:04:34,084
Sir... I have only 50 rupees.

1576
01:04:35,084 --> 01:04:36,209
50 rupees?

1577
01:04:36,709 --> 01:04:37,792
Idiot.

1578
01:04:37,793 --> 01:04:39,543
- How many army personnel?
- Check, check.

1579
01:04:40,668 --> 01:04:42,583
[military march]

1580
01:04:42,584 --> 01:04:43,959
Twelve men.

1581
01:04:45,251 --> 01:04:46,709
Two women.

1582
01:04:47,334 --> 01:04:48,834
And a child as well.

1583
01:04:49,251 --> 01:04:52,626
The Indian army is vacationing
with family and kids.

1584
01:04:53,293 --> 01:04:57,501
It's a good thing we gave guns
and grenades to Abdullah.

1585
01:04:58,376 --> 01:05:02,043
Abdullah, what's in your hand?

1586
01:05:02,459 --> 01:05:03,793
Radio phone, sir.

1587
01:05:04,084 --> 01:05:05,625
In your other hand.

1588
01:05:05,626 --> 01:05:09,084
- In my other hand...
- It's power. Pure power.

1589
01:05:09,376 --> 01:05:10,084
Custard apple?

1590
01:05:10,209 --> 01:05:11,751
Use it.

1591
01:05:11,918 --> 01:05:13,500
Throw it at them.

1592
01:05:13,501 --> 01:05:15,083
Throw a custard apple?

1593
01:05:15,084 --> 01:05:16,709
If he says, then throw it.

1594
01:05:17,043 --> 01:05:18,584
[kissing sound]

1595
01:05:19,834 --> 01:05:21,834
[tense music]

1596
01:05:22,126 --> 01:05:24,126
[mechanical whirring]

1597
01:05:24,543 --> 01:05:26,543
[explosion]

1598
01:05:29,668 --> 01:05:31,168
Custard apple exploded!

1599
01:05:31,334 --> 01:05:32,708
And exploded how?

1600
01:05:32,709 --> 01:05:34,209
[cheering]

1601
01:05:36,334 --> 01:05:38,418
Hey... what was that?

1602
01:05:38,543 --> 01:05:41,708
Nothing. Just like mic testing,
this was blast testing.

1603
01:05:41,709 --> 01:05:43,084
Dominic must have sat
on it again by mistake.

1604
01:05:43,209 --> 01:05:45,667
Oh, wow!

1605
01:05:45,668 --> 01:05:47,084
Let's go.

1606
01:05:48,001 --> 01:05:49,793
[ominous music]

1607
01:05:49,918 --> 01:05:51,418
General Vikram Singh

1608
01:05:52,084 --> 01:05:54,168
Sir. Zatara.

1609
01:05:54,293 --> 01:05:56,293
[intense music]

1610
01:05:58,376 --> 01:05:59,333
Yup.

1611
01:05:59,334 --> 01:06:02,043
I'm sure you heard the blast.

1612
01:06:02,501 --> 01:06:03,333
What blast?

1613
01:06:03,334 --> 01:06:06,708
You caught four of our men
from the Burhan border.

1614
01:06:06,709 --> 01:06:08,418
<i>And now you sent the army.</i>

1615
01:06:08,668 --> 01:06:09,334
Army?

1616
01:06:09,584 --> 01:06:10,834
- Balbeer.
- Sir.

1617
01:06:11,084 --> 01:06:12,959
Did you send any units from here?

1618
01:06:13,168 --> 01:06:13,959
No, sir.

1619
01:06:15,209 --> 01:06:17,084
Then, which unit is he talking about?

1620
01:06:18,251 --> 01:06:21,250
<i>Zatara, you run anti-national operations
from no-man's land?</i>

1621
01:06:21,251 --> 01:06:23,084
<i>and hold villagers hostage?</i>

1622
01:06:23,543 --> 01:06:25,959
<i>If the UN hadn't tied our hands,</i>

1623
01:06:26,084 --> 01:06:28,084
<i>I'd have crushed that misconception.</i>

1624
01:06:28,251 --> 01:06:30,376
You guys are delusional.

1625
01:06:30,834 --> 01:06:35,876
If my demands are not
met by 5:30 pm today...

1626
01:06:36,043 --> 01:06:38,084
If my men are not released,

1627
01:06:38,293 --> 01:06:46,168
then the people of Azadganj will die
just like your soldiers did.

1628
01:06:47,418 --> 01:06:49,043
Which soldiers did he kill?

1629
01:06:49,543 --> 01:06:51,043
Which soldiers did he kill?

1630
01:06:51,668 --> 01:06:54,918
[intense music]

1631
01:07:01,043 --> 01:07:02,668
Who are these people?

1632
01:07:03,334 --> 01:07:04,584
Are they actors as well?

1633
01:07:05,043 --> 01:07:06,209
The Indian army survived.

1634
01:07:06,334 --> 01:07:08,834
According to the script,
these people are terrorists.

1635
01:07:09,209 --> 01:07:10,043
Take charge.

1636
01:07:11,334 --> 01:07:12,251
Let's go, everyone.

1637
01:07:12,418 --> 01:07:14,418
[mysterious music]

1638
01:07:15,668 --> 01:07:17,459
- Look ahead.
- I know that.

1639
01:07:17,793 --> 01:07:19,584
Aren't you a terrorist?

1640
01:07:20,501 --> 01:07:22,168
- You came here to kill us, didn't you?
- Yes.

1641
01:07:22,334 --> 01:07:24,292
Don't just stand there like a loser.

1642
01:07:24,293 --> 01:07:27,959
He looks like Abdullah
Whose gate crashed a wedding.

1643
01:07:29,043 --> 01:07:29,876
He knows my name.

1644
01:07:30,043 --> 01:07:32,043
- Hey... what are you hiding?
- Show me.

1645
01:07:32,209 --> 01:07:33,084
What are you hiding?

1646
01:07:33,209 --> 01:07:34,417
- You're a terrorist, aren't you?
- Yes.

1647
01:07:34,418 --> 01:07:36,376
- Then shoot me here.
- No, no.

1648
01:07:36,501 --> 01:07:39,084
- Alright, shoot me here.
- No, no.

1649
01:07:39,209 --> 01:07:40,167
Shoot me.

1650
01:07:40,168 --> 01:07:41,417
Don't shoot him. Shoot me.

1651
01:07:41,418 --> 01:07:43,083
I have 35 years of experience.

1652
01:07:43,084 --> 01:07:44,334
Action! Cut!

1653
01:07:44,501 --> 01:07:45,501
Action! Cut!

1654
01:07:45,626 --> 01:07:47,708
Action! Cut!

1655
01:07:47,709 --> 01:07:48,667
Forgive us.

1656
01:07:48,668 --> 01:07:50,251
We are villagers.
We were led astray.

1657
01:07:50,418 --> 01:07:52,708
From now on, we'll fight together.

1658
01:07:52,709 --> 01:07:54,042
- Long live the Indian Army!
- He's a good actor.

1659
01:07:54,043 --> 01:07:55,084
Down with Zatara!

1660
01:07:55,251 --> 01:07:56,709
Long live the Indian Army.

1661
01:07:56,876 --> 01:07:59,334
- Down with Zatara!
- I think the villain's name is Zatara.

1662
01:07:59,459 --> 01:08:02,959
Zatara. Sounds better
than Mogambo and Gabbar.

1663
01:08:03,084 --> 01:08:04,083
Hands off.

1664
01:08:04,084 --> 01:08:07,875
Together with you,
we'll set Azadganj free.

1665
01:08:07,876 --> 01:08:10,209
But first, you've got to stand up
and show us Azadganj.

1666
01:08:10,334 --> 01:08:11,750
- Yes, let's go.
- Come on.

1667
01:08:11,751 --> 01:08:13,375
Come here this way.

1668
01:08:13,376 --> 01:08:15,376
[eagle screeches]

1669
01:08:17,626 --> 01:08:19,250
[running footsteps]

1670
01:08:19,251 --> 01:08:20,168
This way.

1671
01:08:21,751 --> 01:08:23,751
[intense music]

1672
01:08:24,584 --> 01:08:25,918
Run!

1673
01:08:28,459 --> 01:08:30,125
Run, they are here again.

1674
01:08:30,126 --> 01:08:32,418
Run run fast

1675
01:08:32,959 --> 01:08:34,751
Go inside. Go inside.
Close the door.

1676
01:08:35,584 --> 01:08:38,001
- [door slams]
- [goat bleats]

1677
01:08:38,959 --> 01:08:41,376
[ominous music]

1678
01:08:47,001 --> 01:08:49,001
[mysterious music]

1679
01:08:54,501 --> 01:08:55,709
- [honking sound]
- Hey.

1680
01:08:56,084 --> 01:08:57,959
Why did you stop?
Did you run into a signal?

1681
01:09:00,251 --> 01:09:01,833
[laughter]

1682
01:09:01,834 --> 01:09:02,959
I don't want to do this film.

1683
01:09:03,584 --> 01:09:05,668
Brother. We're getting millions.

1684
01:09:06,459 --> 01:09:08,251
Money always changes my mind.

1685
01:09:10,668 --> 01:09:12,668
[mysterious music]

1686
01:09:16,668 --> 01:09:18,209
The location is very authentic.

1687
01:09:18,459 --> 01:09:19,542
Where are all the actors?

1688
01:09:19,543 --> 01:09:22,751
Villagers. You are all mistaken.

1689
01:09:23,168 --> 01:09:24,834
They are not Zatara's men.

1690
01:09:25,209 --> 01:09:27,292
The Indian army is here to help us.

1691
01:09:27,293 --> 01:09:28,626
Come out.

1692
01:09:28,918 --> 01:09:30,001
Come out.

1693
01:09:30,251 --> 01:09:31,209
Don't be scared.

1694
01:09:31,751 --> 01:09:33,375
Come on. They are here for us.

1695
01:09:33,376 --> 01:09:34,418
Come on.

1696
01:09:34,751 --> 01:09:35,793
Everyone, come out.

1697
01:09:36,501 --> 01:09:38,501
[intense music]

1698
01:09:42,959 --> 01:09:44,959
[hopeful music]

1699
01:09:50,626 --> 01:09:52,626
[hopeful music continues]

1700
01:10:02,293 --> 01:10:04,293
[hopeful music continues]

1701
01:10:08,793 --> 01:10:10,625
[camera beeps]

1702
01:10:10,626 --> 01:10:12,209
Brother, look at the crowd.

1703
01:10:13,084 --> 01:10:15,251
It's really good casting.
The characters look authentic.

1704
01:10:16,084 --> 01:10:17,084
Authentic.

1705
01:10:17,501 --> 01:10:20,209
Auntie... The Indian army.

1706
01:10:21,001 --> 01:10:22,418
I don't believe it.

1707
01:10:22,668 --> 01:10:23,959
He even cast old folks.

1708
01:10:24,918 --> 01:10:26,543
Hats off to Dev-Das.

1709
01:10:26,793 --> 01:10:27,668
Villagers...

1710
01:10:28,334 --> 01:10:29,918
God has answered our prayers.

1711
01:10:30,251 --> 01:10:31,750
We both were fools

1712
01:10:31,751 --> 01:10:34,168
to side with Zatara.

1713
01:10:34,418 --> 01:10:36,834
But now we have realised our mistake.

1714
01:10:36,959 --> 01:10:37,583
Yes.

1715
01:10:37,584 --> 01:10:40,668
The Indian army made
us realise our mistake.

1716
01:10:40,793 --> 01:10:44,083
They have come to free Azadganj.

1717
01:10:44,084 --> 01:10:45,376
You guys come now...

1718
01:10:45,543 --> 01:10:47,375
[solemn music]

1719
01:10:47,376 --> 01:10:48,918
Finally, you remembered us...

1720
01:10:49,043 --> 01:10:51,043
[beeping]

1721
01:10:52,001 --> 01:10:53,293
After so much bloodshed,

1722
01:10:53,626 --> 01:10:57,084
dead bodies and violence?

1723
01:10:57,959 --> 01:10:59,084
And you guys show up now.

1724
01:10:59,251 --> 01:11:02,709
We've been waiting for ages.

1725
01:11:02,876 --> 01:11:04,168
And you think of us now.

1726
01:11:05,793 --> 01:11:08,459
We've been living a life of humiliation.

1727
01:11:08,751 --> 01:11:10,583
[awkward music]

1728
01:11:10,584 --> 01:11:11,918
We've been suffering

1729
01:11:12,084 --> 01:11:13,959
and starving to death every minute.

1730
01:11:14,084 --> 01:11:16,084
[burping sound]

1731
01:11:16,209 --> 01:11:17,043
Sorry.

1732
01:11:18,251 --> 01:11:19,251
What did he eat?

1733
01:11:19,876 --> 01:11:21,959
If she says all the dialogues,

1734
01:11:22,626 --> 01:11:24,001
what am I doing in the film?

1735
01:11:25,209 --> 01:11:26,084
Glamour!

1736
01:11:26,709 --> 01:11:29,168
Have you come to bury our bodies?

1737
01:11:30,043 --> 01:11:31,209
You gave her such a nice role.

1738
01:11:31,334 --> 01:11:32,292
She will overshadow all of us.

1739
01:11:32,293 --> 01:11:34,167
She's a legend.

1740
01:11:34,168 --> 01:11:36,083
Look, you are mis--

1741
01:11:36,084 --> 01:11:38,043
See what? See what?

1742
01:11:38,168 --> 01:11:39,459
- My hair.
- See what?

1743
01:11:39,918 --> 01:11:40,876
What an actor.

1744
01:11:41,293 --> 01:11:42,668
Where were you?

1745
01:11:44,001 --> 01:11:45,459
20 years have passed.

1746
01:11:46,584 --> 01:11:47,584
And you show up now.

1747
01:11:47,751 --> 01:11:49,751
[instrumental music]

1748
01:11:50,084 --> 01:11:52,709
Where were you these past 20 years?

1749
01:11:53,293 --> 01:11:54,084
You're overdoing it now.

1750
01:11:54,251 --> 01:11:55,209
Down. Down.

1751
01:11:55,334 --> 01:11:56,084
Overdoing...

1752
01:11:56,376 --> 01:11:57,334
Overdoing what?

1753
01:11:58,001 --> 01:11:59,501
This is not our frustration.

1754
01:12:00,376 --> 01:12:03,834
It is our bane
that cries out through this plea.

1755
01:12:04,709 --> 01:12:05,834
Overdoing?

1756
01:12:05,959 --> 01:12:07,959
[spits]

1757
01:12:08,251 --> 01:12:09,043
Why that...

1758
01:12:09,209 --> 01:12:10,334
Method acting.

1759
01:12:10,501 --> 01:12:11,668
She's spitting on my shoe.

1760
01:12:11,793 --> 01:12:12,668
Method acting.

1761
01:12:13,084 --> 01:12:14,584
Stop it, Zoya. Stop it.

1762
01:12:14,959 --> 01:12:16,334
[gibberish]

1763
01:12:19,918 --> 01:12:21,918
[gibberish continues]

1764
01:12:24,959 --> 01:12:25,918
What is she saying?

1765
01:12:27,584 --> 01:12:29,584
[gibberish continues]

1766
01:12:31,626 --> 01:12:33,333
Either she's a really good actor

1767
01:12:33,334 --> 01:12:35,209
or she doesn't remember her dialogues.

1768
01:12:35,376 --> 01:12:37,375
[gibberish continues]

1769
01:12:37,376 --> 01:12:38,918
Auntie is absolutely right.

1770
01:12:39,043 --> 01:12:40,292
[awkward music]

1771
01:12:40,293 --> 01:12:41,251
Absolutely right.

1772
01:12:42,084 --> 01:12:43,459
How did he understand?

1773
01:12:44,834 --> 01:12:46,834
[groaning]

1774
01:12:48,584 --> 01:12:50,584
Where is the sound coming from?

1775
01:12:52,584 --> 01:12:53,543
Over there.

1776
01:12:54,876 --> 01:12:56,876
[labored breathing]

1777
01:13:02,793 --> 01:13:04,334
Why is he tied up?

1778
01:13:04,834 --> 01:13:06,084
It's because of Zatara.

1779
01:13:07,293 --> 01:13:09,084
Zatara gave strict instructions,

1780
01:13:09,668 --> 01:13:13,293
that this well of Azadganj
is off limits for us.

1781
01:13:13,501 --> 01:13:17,084
And yet this innocent child
tried to drink water from that well

1782
01:13:17,251 --> 01:13:19,293
and Zatara tied him up

1783
01:13:19,834 --> 01:13:23,376
and gave orders to let him starve.

1784
01:13:24,834 --> 01:13:28,251
[arabic language]

1785
01:13:28,376 --> 01:13:30,376
[awkward music]

1786
01:13:30,501 --> 01:13:31,876
What are you looking up for?

1787
01:13:32,376 --> 01:13:34,709
Everything he's saying
is going over my head.

1788
01:13:35,793 --> 01:13:38,167
Hey, specy. Keep this 4500.

1789
01:13:38,168 --> 01:13:39,209
Keep the camera on me.

1790
01:13:39,376 --> 01:13:40,459
I'm going to say my dialogue.

1791
01:13:40,834 --> 01:13:42,834
[clears throat]

1792
01:13:43,168 --> 01:13:44,542
But who are you, mister?

1793
01:13:44,543 --> 01:13:46,417
I've got your money from earlier.

1794
01:13:46,418 --> 01:13:48,042
[comic music]

1795
01:13:48,043 --> 01:13:49,125
Give me blessings, please.

1796
01:13:49,126 --> 01:13:51,083
[indistinct speech]

1797
01:13:51,084 --> 01:13:52,376
I have understood everything.

1798
01:13:53,084 --> 01:13:54,334
Don't worry.

1799
01:13:54,709 --> 01:13:56,334
No harm will come to this village.

1800
01:13:57,084 --> 01:13:57,834
Zoya...

1801
01:13:58,376 --> 01:14:02,418
I will return those
20 years that you lost.

1802
01:14:03,959 --> 01:14:05,918
And not a single person

1803
01:14:06,084 --> 01:14:09,001
from this village will be
Zatara's pawn anymore.

1804
01:14:10,668 --> 01:14:11,751
Uncle Murad,

1805
01:14:12,376 --> 01:14:15,417
No one will face any consequences.

1806
01:14:15,418 --> 01:14:17,418
[awkward music]

1807
01:14:17,793 --> 01:14:20,417
And the one to offer water
to this helpless...

1808
01:14:20,418 --> 01:14:21,334
Will be me.

1809
01:14:22,668 --> 01:14:24,668
[tense music]

1810
01:14:26,959 --> 01:14:28,418
He's eating up my scene.

1811
01:14:28,709 --> 01:14:30,083
He's not eating anything.
He's offering water.

1812
01:14:30,084 --> 01:14:30,959
Stay on the mark.

1813
01:14:33,626 --> 01:14:36,126
[groaning]

1814
01:14:37,376 --> 01:14:39,334
We're not allowed
to take water from that well.

1815
01:14:39,459 --> 01:14:41,584
That is Zatara's well.

1816
01:14:41,709 --> 01:14:42,834
Villagers...

1817
01:14:43,084 --> 01:14:45,793
Do you want to fill the bucket
from the well

1818
01:14:46,168 --> 01:14:48,584
or with your tears?

1819
01:14:50,084 --> 01:14:53,293
[lock breaks]

1820
01:14:56,209 --> 01:14:59,042
- Where is that?
- What, mister?

1821
01:14:59,043 --> 01:15:00,584
Who am I asking?

1822
01:15:00,793 --> 01:15:04,750
Listen... what's that thing
that's near the well?

1823
01:15:04,751 --> 01:15:05,458
Thirsty guy?

1824
01:15:05,459 --> 01:15:07,501
The thirsty guy is right here.

1825
01:15:07,709 --> 01:15:11,084
The thing that stays bent
over the well like this.

1826
01:15:11,293 --> 01:15:12,043
Horse.

1827
01:15:12,168 --> 01:15:13,501
Not a horse, you idiot.

1828
01:15:14,626 --> 01:15:18,334
I'll hit you guys with this bucket.

1829
01:15:18,543 --> 01:15:20,792
It's that thing in your hand.

1830
01:15:20,793 --> 01:15:22,251
Anna, Bucket.

1831
01:15:22,418 --> 01:15:24,626
Bucket it was.

1832
01:15:24,918 --> 01:15:28,376
Sir, give me some water.

1833
01:15:28,543 --> 01:15:30,292
Of course. Of course.

1834
01:15:30,293 --> 01:15:32,000
[camera beeps]

1835
01:15:32,001 --> 01:15:36,543
Now this soldier's going to
give this thirsty man some water.

1836
01:15:36,709 --> 01:15:39,584
Me too. I'll give him some water.

1837
01:15:39,918 --> 01:15:41,209
Me too. Me too.

1838
01:15:41,334 --> 01:15:42,833
Who else wants to give him water?

1839
01:15:42,834 --> 01:15:44,209
Give me the water.
