These guys are dons.

2356
01:42:56,584 --> 01:42:58,793
What are you guys doing?

2357
01:42:59,001 --> 01:43:00,625
Go and fight Zatara.

2358
01:43:00,626 --> 01:43:03,208
I won't interfere
in this scene, nor the fight.

2359
01:43:03,209 --> 01:43:05,918
You can even keep these
two heroines if you want.

2360
01:43:06,168 --> 01:43:07,709
You decide everything.

2361
01:43:07,834 --> 01:43:09,125
And don't touch my hair.

2362
01:43:09,126 --> 01:43:10,668
Are you guys crazy?

2363
01:43:11,459 --> 01:43:13,000
There's a difference between
dons and terrorists.

2364
01:43:13,001 --> 01:43:17,084
We use bombs, but these guys
blow themselves up.

2365
01:43:18,376 --> 01:43:21,126
We shoot first and then talk.

2366
01:43:21,293 --> 01:43:23,792
- But they shoot first...
- And then talk?

2367
01:43:23,793 --> 01:43:27,209
No... they shoot first
and then shoot some more.

2368
01:43:27,418 --> 01:43:29,168
But when do they talk?

2369
01:43:29,668 --> 01:43:31,084
Will you shut up?

2370
01:43:33,834 --> 01:43:34,918
We are dons.

2371
01:43:35,084 --> 01:43:36,709
He's a terrorist.

2372
01:43:38,959 --> 01:43:42,167
Mister, you were over there.

2373
01:43:42,168 --> 01:43:43,125
How did you get here so quickly?

2374
01:43:43,126 --> 01:43:44,043
Not fair.

2375
01:43:44,209 --> 01:43:47,251
Alright, fine, we'll go over there.
Let's go.

2376
01:43:47,418 --> 01:43:49,168
[funny music]

2377
01:43:49,668 --> 01:43:52,001
[suspensful music]

2378
01:43:53,418 --> 01:43:57,293
Dev-Das... it's your responsibility
to take us back alive.

2379
01:43:57,459 --> 01:43:59,208
One of you go talk to him.

2380
01:43:59,209 --> 01:44:01,918
Das, you're the eldest.
You go talk to him.

2381
01:44:02,584 --> 01:44:04,043
Yes, Das. You go.

2382
01:44:04,334 --> 01:44:07,584
You go. Confidence.
Confidence.

2383
01:44:07,959 --> 01:44:09,626
- All the best.
- Come on.

2384
01:44:10,959 --> 01:44:13,126
Zatara. Let me explain.

2385
01:44:13,251 --> 01:44:14,042
Go ahead.

2386
01:44:14,043 --> 01:44:16,584
I think you are confused.

2387
01:44:16,793 --> 01:44:19,001
Let me clear your confusion.

2388
01:44:19,376 --> 01:44:23,668
There are two kinds
of clouds in the sky.

2389
01:44:24,459 --> 01:44:27,418
The ones that rain...
and the ones that thunder.

2390
01:44:27,834 --> 01:44:31,459
The clouds that bring rain
never thunder.

2391
01:44:31,668 --> 01:44:34,376
They just rain.

2392
01:44:36,584 --> 01:44:38,834
[confusing music]

2393
01:44:39,501 --> 01:44:41,334
- And...
- And what?

2394
01:44:41,626 --> 01:44:43,668
You said there are
two kinds of clouds.

2395
01:44:43,793 --> 01:44:44,751
The ones that rain don't thunder.

2396
01:44:45,168 --> 01:44:48,168
What about the ones
that thunder?

2397
01:44:48,376 --> 01:44:49,833
They just thunder.

2398
01:44:49,834 --> 01:44:50,667
One rains...

2399
01:44:50,668 --> 01:44:52,251
Why did you send him?

2400
01:44:52,501 --> 01:44:53,917
How's he supposed to explain anything?

2401
01:44:53,918 --> 01:44:54,500
Why?

2402
01:44:54,501 --> 01:44:56,834
He still hasn't managed
to explain his own film.

2403
01:44:57,376 --> 01:44:59,543
- The cloud that rains.
- Correct.

2404
01:44:59,668 --> 01:45:03,917
The cloud which thunders, only thunders.

2405
01:45:03,918 --> 01:45:06,459
Zatara sir. Zatara sir. Zatara sir.

2406
01:45:06,626 --> 01:45:08,584
Please don't listen to him.

2407
01:45:08,751 --> 01:45:11,626
I will explain the entire
situation in two minutes.

2408
01:45:12,001 --> 01:45:13,626
[wind sound]

2409
01:45:14,168 --> 01:45:15,793
Can you hear anything?

2410
01:45:18,043 --> 01:45:18,918
It's as simple as that.

2411
01:45:19,043 --> 01:45:20,333
That's all.

2412
01:45:20,334 --> 01:45:22,083
I explained everything. Come on.

2413
01:45:22,084 --> 01:45:23,626
Everything will be alright.

2414
01:45:24,209 --> 01:45:24,959
What's wrong with you?

2415
01:45:25,084 --> 01:45:25,876
How can everything be fine?

2416
01:45:26,043 --> 01:45:26,876
Explained to him what?

2417
01:45:27,126 --> 01:45:28,459
You should have given him
in writing instead.

2418
01:45:29,126 --> 01:45:30,418
You didn't say a word to him.

2419
01:45:30,709 --> 01:45:32,043
Who will go explain to him next?

2420
01:45:33,126 --> 01:45:36,334
Who will go?
who will become the scapegoat?

2421
01:45:36,459 --> 01:45:38,459
Someone please.

2422
01:45:40,001 --> 01:45:42,001
[suspenseful music]

2423
01:45:42,918 --> 01:45:44,459
Paa ji, you go explain to him.

2424
01:45:44,584 --> 01:45:45,667
Even your name is Diler.

2425
01:45:45,668 --> 01:45:46,376
What Daler?

2426
01:45:46,626 --> 01:45:50,418
Calling oneself Diler doesn't
make anyone brave.

2427
01:45:50,584 --> 01:45:52,459
Names don't mean a thing.

2428
01:45:52,668 --> 01:45:56,792
My wife's name is Shanti,
but she keeps chattering all the time.

2429
01:45:56,793 --> 01:45:58,458
Her sister's name is Sharmili,

2430
01:45:58,459 --> 01:46:00,834
but I've never come across anyone
as shameless as she.

2431
01:46:00,959 --> 01:46:03,250
I have a friend called Aakash
but he lives on the ground floor.

2432
01:46:03,251 --> 01:46:04,209
You're absolutely right.

2433
01:46:04,793 --> 01:46:05,668
And this bloody blind guy.

2434
01:46:05,793 --> 01:46:08,125
He can't see a thing
but his name is Nainsukh.

2435
01:46:08,126 --> 01:46:09,376
Names don't mean a thing.

2436
01:46:09,501 --> 01:46:11,125
You like to be Daler, don't you?

2437
01:46:11,126 --> 01:46:12,084
Then you go be Daler.

2438
01:46:12,209 --> 01:46:12,875
Go and fight.

2439
01:46:12,876 --> 01:46:14,583
His name is Daler
and mine is Mehendi.

2440
01:46:14,584 --> 01:46:15,376
Go and fight.

2441
01:46:16,168 --> 01:46:17,168
Congratulations!

2442
01:46:18,793 --> 01:46:19,293
Wow.

2443
01:46:19,418 --> 01:46:21,626
Everyone's clapping,
but who will go there?

2444
01:46:21,876 --> 01:46:22,709
You go!

2445
01:46:22,876 --> 01:46:24,251
You are sending everyone else to die.

2446
01:46:24,418 --> 01:46:26,543
You are International
Khiladi (international player).

2447
01:46:26,751 --> 01:46:27,668
So go talk to them.

2448
01:46:28,126 --> 01:46:29,209
You can do it.

2449
01:46:29,793 --> 01:46:30,376
Go.

2450
01:46:30,709 --> 01:46:31,376
Alright.

2451
01:46:33,459 --> 01:46:34,250
I'll go.

2452
01:46:34,251 --> 01:46:35,751
- Go on.
- I am going.

2453
01:46:35,918 --> 01:46:36,918
No, brother.

2454
01:46:37,584 --> 01:46:39,376
[crying]

2455
01:46:41,459 --> 01:46:44,668
[suspenseful music]

2456
01:46:46,459 --> 01:46:48,501
Either we survive, or he dies.

2457
01:46:49,418 --> 01:46:52,418
Sire... I am not a soldier.

2458
01:46:52,543 --> 01:46:54,000
I'm not a soldier.

2459
01:46:54,001 --> 01:46:56,126
We are flop actors, sir.

2460
01:46:56,626 --> 01:46:57,709
Flop actors?

2461
01:46:59,126 --> 01:47:00,418
Flop actors?

2462
01:47:01,251 --> 01:47:04,917
We were told everything
would be fake.

2463
01:47:04,918 --> 01:47:08,626
But when you shot him,
we realised it was all real.

2464
01:47:08,793 --> 01:47:10,333
Forgive us.

2465
01:47:10,334 --> 01:47:12,793
And do you know
who brought us here?

2466
01:47:12,959 --> 01:47:14,793
These two.
These two.

2467
01:47:14,918 --> 01:47:16,918
These two.
These two.

2468
01:47:17,043 --> 01:47:18,708
These two brought us here.

2469
01:47:18,709 --> 01:47:19,834
They don't know anything.

2470
01:47:19,959 --> 01:47:21,626
Let me tell you one more thing.

2471
01:47:22,168 --> 01:47:24,043
Four of your men showed up
in the morning.

2472
01:47:24,168 --> 01:47:25,126
You sent them.

2473
01:47:25,251 --> 01:47:27,084
Do you know who beat them up?

2474
01:47:27,376 --> 01:47:29,292
Them... these two beat them up.

2475
01:47:29,293 --> 01:47:30,125
These two.

2476
01:47:30,126 --> 01:47:31,083
- These two beat him up.
- What are you doing?

2477
01:47:31,084 --> 01:47:32,543
- Rajeev, please...
- They call themselves dons, sir.

2478
01:47:33,084 --> 01:47:35,208
Sir... what do you mean
what's it called?

2479
01:47:35,209 --> 01:47:36,918
I'll tell Zatara everything.

2480
01:47:37,084 --> 01:47:39,125
- I am on your team. Leave me.
- How will you save us?

2481
01:47:39,126 --> 01:47:40,668
They beat him up, sir.

2482
01:47:40,793 --> 01:47:41,709
And sir...

2483
01:47:42,376 --> 01:47:46,626
we've got nothing to do
with patriotism, country, or soil.

2484
01:47:47,126 --> 01:47:48,751
You want to spread terror, right?

2485
01:47:48,959 --> 01:47:49,918
Let me show you.

2486
01:47:50,418 --> 01:47:52,876
Kill all the villagers.
Kill all of them!

2487
01:47:53,501 --> 01:47:54,626
- Kill us.
- Kill them all.

2488
01:47:54,834 --> 01:47:57,793
And sir, kill this man first.

2489
01:47:58,168 --> 01:48:00,376
Kill this old man, sir.

2490
01:48:00,543 --> 01:48:03,292
No one understands
what this man says in Urdu.

2491
01:48:03,293 --> 01:48:04,542
What is the point
of having language?

2492
01:48:04,543 --> 01:48:05,376
To understand each other.

2493
01:48:05,501 --> 01:48:07,626
But we can't understand a thing he says.

2494
01:48:07,793 --> 01:48:09,792
Even God would
need subtitles for his Urdu.

2495
01:48:09,793 --> 01:48:10,875
He is right, bhai.

2496
01:48:10,876 --> 01:48:12,292
We can't understand a thing.

2497
01:48:12,293 --> 01:48:15,542
"Auntie is right."

2498
01:48:15,543 --> 01:48:16,668
What she's right!

2499
01:48:16,834 --> 01:48:17,834
And next...

2500
01:48:18,209 --> 01:48:19,251
Where is that old woman?

2501
01:48:19,376 --> 01:48:21,209
Kill this old woman.

2502
01:48:21,584 --> 01:48:22,584
She is crazy.

2503
01:48:22,709 --> 01:48:26,126
What she says, why she says
or what for, no one understands.

2504
01:48:27,459 --> 01:48:28,334
[gibberish]

2505
01:48:28,543 --> 01:48:30,376
No one can understand
what she is saying.

2506
01:48:30,501 --> 01:48:32,251
She has bloody faucets fitted
in her eyes.

2507
01:48:32,418 --> 01:48:34,543
I want to punch her in the gut.

2508
01:48:34,793 --> 01:48:35,583
Exactly, bhai.

2509
01:48:35,584 --> 01:48:36,543
Then finally we'll hear her voice.

2510
01:48:36,751 --> 01:48:37,543
And then...

2511
01:48:38,418 --> 01:48:39,668
kill her next.

2512
01:48:40,084 --> 01:48:41,959
She cuts everyone's dialogue,

2513
01:48:42,168 --> 01:48:44,626
their fingers, and then she spits, sir!

2514
01:48:44,793 --> 01:48:46,917
She has no civic sense, sir.

2515
01:48:46,918 --> 01:48:48,250
She spreads germs, sir.

2516
01:48:48,251 --> 01:48:49,209
Full of germs.

2517
01:48:49,334 --> 01:48:50,126
Kill...

2518
01:48:52,209 --> 01:48:55,168
Sir... don't be angry.

2519
01:48:55,334 --> 01:48:56,876
Don't be angry, sir.

2520
01:48:57,459 --> 01:48:58,834
Let us go, sir.

2521
01:48:58,959 --> 01:49:00,042
We're clowns.

2522
01:49:00,043 --> 01:49:01,833
We act for a living, sire.

2523
01:49:01,834 --> 01:49:03,959
We perform stunts for money.

2524
01:49:04,126 --> 01:49:07,168
- We sing, dance...
- Dance?

2525
01:49:07,543 --> 01:49:09,043
Do you like dancing?

2526
01:49:09,334 --> 01:49:10,168
Show me.

2527
01:49:10,293 --> 01:49:12,376
Manicure, pedicure. Come on.

2528
01:49:12,543 --> 01:49:13,708
- Come here. Quickly.
- Is he calling us?

2529
01:49:13,709 --> 01:49:15,376
Go on, he's calling.

2530
01:49:15,543 --> 01:49:16,584
We'll show you our dance right away.

2531
01:49:16,709 --> 01:49:17,376
Don't mind.

2532
01:49:18,043 --> 01:49:19,333
<i>♪ That tall, towering frame ♪</i>

2533
01:49:19,334 --> 01:49:20,708
<i>♪ and then you're stunning
beyond compare ♪</i>

2534
01:49:20,709 --> 01:49:23,876
<i>♪ Your body dazzles and shines ♪</i>

2535
01:49:26,168 --> 01:49:28,626
<i>♪ you're the one I'm crazy for ♪</i>

2536
01:49:31,376 --> 01:49:34,959
<i>♪ You're the one I'm crazy for ♪</i>

2537
01:49:36,543 --> 01:49:37,668
Wait. Stop.

2538
01:49:37,918 --> 01:49:39,543
Stop...
He's getting angry.

2539
01:49:39,793 --> 01:49:41,459
Sir, should we show you something else?

2540
01:49:42,293 --> 01:49:43,709
Song... would you like to hear a song?

2541
01:49:43,959 --> 01:49:45,751
- Okay.
- Daler ji. Daler ji.

2542
01:49:45,918 --> 01:49:47,543
Daler ji. Daler ji.

2543
01:49:47,668 --> 01:49:49,918
- Come over here.
- Daler ji.

2544
01:49:50,126 --> 01:49:52,834
You must have heard about him...
he's popular.

2545
01:49:52,959 --> 01:49:54,043
Daler Mehendi.

2546
01:49:54,293 --> 01:49:55,334
Sing now!

2547
01:49:55,543 --> 01:49:58,001
♪

2548
01:49:58,459 --> 01:49:59,543
Not a sad song.

2549
01:50:00,418 --> 01:50:03,584
[singing]

2550
01:50:10,793 --> 01:50:15,167
<i>♪ Listen, Zatara chief,
we don't know what says this Sardar ♪</i>

2551
01:50:15,168 --> 01:50:16,917
<i>♪ We're just petty artists ♪</i>

2552
01:50:16,918 --> 01:50:19,542
<i>♪ forgive us, sir ♪</i>

2553
01:50:19,543 --> 01:50:22,167
<i>♪ We have one wife, four kids ♪</i>

2554
01:50:22,168 --> 01:50:23,958
<i>♪ There's darkness before our eyes ♪</i>

2555
01:50:23,959 --> 01:50:31,209
<i>♪ we're TV artists and Bhojpuri artists ♪</i>

2556
01:50:31,918 --> 01:50:34,959
<i>♪ Let us go ♪</i>

2557
01:50:41,543 --> 01:50:43,334
Rabbits!

2558
01:50:43,709 --> 01:50:46,168
He took out a bomb. Bomb!

2559
01:50:48,168 --> 01:50:52,084
[dramtaic music]

2560
01:50:56,334 --> 01:50:59,709
[dramtaic music continues]

2561
01:51:01,751 --> 01:51:04,459
[laughing]

2562
01:51:06,626 --> 01:51:07,959
He's happy. He's happy.

2563
01:51:09,793 --> 01:51:12,126
Your face looks familiar.

2564
01:51:12,668 --> 01:51:14,501
We just met a while ago.

2565
01:51:14,793 --> 01:51:17,375
Zatara sir. Do you watch flop films too?

2566
01:51:17,376 --> 01:51:17,959
Shut up.

2567
01:51:19,709 --> 01:51:22,584
I am laughing at you guys, not them.

2568
01:51:23,209 --> 01:51:26,209
You were trying to act brave
by trusting these people.

2569
01:51:27,043 --> 01:51:29,168
They are clowns! Bloody clowns!

2570
01:51:32,209 --> 01:51:34,959
No, no...

2571
01:51:35,209 --> 01:51:36,334
Stop, Zatara.

2572
01:51:36,668 --> 01:51:37,709
Don't kill them!

2573
01:51:37,876 --> 01:51:38,959
They are innocent.

2574
01:51:39,959 --> 01:51:42,418
I'm ready to go with you.

2575
01:51:42,834 --> 01:51:44,751
No, no, Zoya.

2576
01:51:45,376 --> 01:51:47,959
Why are you surprised, Zatara?

2577
01:51:49,376 --> 01:51:51,293
Why am I doing this for their sake,

2578
01:51:51,459 --> 01:51:54,876
who neither came for us nor the humanity.

2579
01:51:56,876 --> 01:51:58,418
What is important is

2580
01:51:59,501 --> 01:52:01,250
Because one thing matters

2581
01:52:01,251 --> 01:52:05,293
And if saving their lives
means sacrificing my honour...

2582
01:52:07,334 --> 01:52:08,959
Then I accept this deal.

2583
01:52:09,584 --> 01:52:12,793
Zatara, she is ready
to sacrifice her honour.

2584
01:52:12,959 --> 01:52:14,084
Let us go.

2585
01:52:15,043 --> 01:52:17,208
Signal. Let's go. Come on.

2586
01:52:17,209 --> 01:52:18,376
Thank you.

2587
01:52:20,251 --> 01:52:22,876
[emotional music]

2588
01:52:28,084 --> 01:52:31,543
[emotional music continues]

2589
01:52:38,209 --> 01:52:42,043
[emotional music continues]

2590
01:52:48,168 --> 01:52:51,459
[emotional music continues]

2591
01:52:55,251 --> 01:52:58,209
I'm leaving now,
but I'll be back at 5:30.

2592
01:52:58,459 --> 01:53:00,626
Handle the villagers until then.

2593
01:53:01,959 --> 01:53:03,168
Zoya.

2594
01:53:06,043 --> 01:53:07,293
Be ready.

2595
01:53:09,418 --> 01:53:12,584
[helicopter's sound]

2596
01:53:16,043 --> 01:53:17,001
Come on, guys. Come on.

2597
01:53:17,126 --> 01:53:18,042
We don't have time.

2598
01:53:18,043 --> 01:53:18,959
Helicopter is here.

2599
01:53:20,126 --> 01:53:21,375
Remember what I told you?

2600
01:53:21,376 --> 01:53:23,500
It's exactly like I told you.

2601
01:53:23,501 --> 01:53:25,458
Our destiny is our destiny,

2602
01:53:25,459 --> 01:53:27,083
and their destiny is their destiny...

2603
01:53:27,084 --> 01:53:29,418
Stop blaming destiny.

2604
01:53:30,584 --> 01:53:34,501
Zoya sacrificing herself for
us was her decision.

2605
01:53:34,709 --> 01:53:38,584
And us running away like
cowards was our decision.

2606
01:53:38,709 --> 01:53:41,084
Everyone knows that
our decision is wrong!

2607
01:53:41,293 --> 01:53:44,126
In our hearts, we all know
what we're doing is wrong.

2608
01:53:44,251 --> 01:53:46,626
I know. I know, but what next?

2609
01:53:46,751 --> 01:53:47,750
What do we do next?

2610
01:53:47,751 --> 01:53:48,958
We'll have to leave.

2611
01:53:48,959 --> 01:53:50,417
Yes, Rajeev is right.

2612
01:53:50,418 --> 01:53:52,084
We'll die if we stay here.

2613
01:53:52,209 --> 01:53:54,043
- We won't go.
- Won't go?

2614
01:53:54,251 --> 01:53:55,418
Are you going to stay here?

2615
01:53:55,709 --> 01:53:57,209
What will we do even if we stay here?

2616
01:53:57,334 --> 01:53:59,375
We'll try to save the villagers.

2617
01:53:59,376 --> 01:54:01,958
For that, we have to fight Zatara.

2618
01:54:01,959 --> 01:54:03,625
He is a real terrorist!

2619
01:54:03,626 --> 01:54:05,542
With real weapons.

2620
01:54:05,543 --> 01:54:07,543
Courage is the biggest weapon.

2621
01:54:07,793 --> 01:54:10,001
Have you lost your mind, Sardar ji?

2622
01:54:10,293 --> 01:54:12,209
Do you want to go
on a suicide mission?

2623
01:54:12,626 --> 01:54:14,500
They are three hundred
and they are only three.

2624
01:54:14,501 --> 01:54:15,668
Not three, but four.

2625
01:54:15,834 --> 01:54:16,750
Four!

2626
01:54:16,751 --> 01:54:18,125
Including Dev, it's five.

2627
01:54:18,126 --> 01:54:20,876
Our father's dreams were
we become a good director.

2628
01:54:21,001 --> 01:54:22,543
Whether we become
good directors or not,

2629
01:54:22,751 --> 01:54:24,584
but we'll definitely
be good human beings.

2630
01:54:24,709 --> 01:54:26,251
- We're not leaving.
- He's right.

2631
01:54:26,418 --> 01:54:27,792
Rather than dying every day

2632
01:54:27,793 --> 01:54:29,625
we would die once
doing a good deed.

2633
01:54:29,626 --> 01:54:31,500
We're not going.
We're also staying.

2634
01:54:31,501 --> 01:54:33,334
What is wrong with all of you?

2635
01:54:33,584 --> 01:54:35,833
Only one... you guys stayed
in that village for only one day,

2636
01:54:35,834 --> 01:54:37,375
and you're ready to give your life.

2637
01:54:37,376 --> 01:54:38,876
Go tell that to Zoya.

2638
01:54:39,084 --> 01:54:40,959
Even she spent one day with us.

2639
01:54:41,084 --> 01:54:44,001
What changed that she was willing
to give her life for us?

2640
01:54:46,751 --> 01:54:48,209
Rajeev... even I am going with them.

2641
01:54:48,501 --> 01:54:50,333
I admit I'm not too bright,

2642
01:54:50,334 --> 01:54:54,459
but at least I know
what's right and wrong.

2643
01:54:54,834 --> 01:54:56,208
Let him go, Jenny.

2644
01:54:56,209 --> 01:54:57,251
Even I am staying.

2645
01:54:57,418 --> 01:54:59,293
Nadia, don't be a fool.

2646
01:54:59,501 --> 01:55:00,917
You were a cheater.

2647
01:55:00,918 --> 01:55:03,126
But I realised what
a coward you are.

2648
01:55:03,793 --> 01:55:06,751
Fine. Die. All of you die.

2649
01:55:06,918 --> 01:55:09,543
- Nainsukh, are you coming?
- I'm staying.

2650
01:55:09,834 --> 01:55:11,833
I admit I'm blind,
but I am not stupid.

2651
01:55:11,834 --> 01:55:13,458
Spare me the lecture.

2652
01:55:13,459 --> 01:55:15,668
Die. All of you die.

2653
01:55:16,001 --> 01:55:16,918
I am going.

2654
01:55:17,084 --> 01:55:20,376
You can either come with me
or stay here and die!

2655
01:55:21,751 --> 01:55:24,626
[dramatic music]

2656
01:55:30,459 --> 01:55:33,709
[dramatic music continues]

2657
01:55:38,376 --> 01:55:40,376
Let's go. Hurry up.
Come on.

2658
01:55:44,834 --> 01:55:48,209
[emotional music]

2659
01:55:51,668 --> 01:55:54,876
They went to save her,
but she's come here herself.

2660
01:55:55,084 --> 01:55:56,251
Do you want to come too?
Let's go.

2661
01:55:56,418 --> 01:55:58,834
Not me, take her.

2662
01:56:01,418 --> 01:56:04,168
I will survive one way or another,

2663
01:56:04,376 --> 01:56:06,959
but she will get a chance
to live her life.

2664
01:56:08,418 --> 01:56:09,501
In the name of God.

2665
01:56:11,918 --> 01:56:14,043
Urvi. Just go.

2666
01:56:14,459 --> 01:56:15,543
I will come to you.

2667
01:56:15,959 --> 01:56:19,084
Go on. Go. Go...

2668
01:56:20,251 --> 01:56:23,001
[emotional music]

2669
01:56:23,918 --> 01:56:24,793
Urvi.

2670
01:56:25,876 --> 01:56:29,084
[emotional music]

2671
01:56:34,376 --> 01:56:37,876
[emotional music continues]

2672
01:56:42,709 --> 01:56:46,626
[emotional music continues]

2673
01:56:51,334 --> 01:56:55,001
[dramatic music]

2674
01:56:57,168 --> 01:56:59,918
[neck breaking sound]

2675
01:57:00,751 --> 01:57:03,001
[dramatic music]

2676
01:57:06,209 --> 01:57:08,959
[fight breaks out]

2677
01:57:12,959 --> 01:57:16,168
[gun firing]

2678
01:57:18,043 --> 01:57:20,793
[intense action music]

2679
01:57:22,334 --> 01:57:23,626
Get out of here quickly!

2680
01:57:24,459 --> 01:57:27,626
[action music]

2681
01:57:31,334 --> 01:57:35,043
[emotional music]

2682
01:57:39,584 --> 01:57:42,959
[blast sound]

2683
01:57:46,709 --> 01:57:50,251
[rapid gunfire]

2684
01:57:51,209 --> 01:57:53,251
[gun trigger sound]

2685
01:57:56,834 --> 01:57:59,668
[dramatic music]

2686
01:58:04,084 --> 01:58:04,709
Hey.

2687
01:58:05,918 --> 01:58:06,751
Let's go.

2688
01:58:09,418 --> 01:58:13,584
Mother! Mother!

2689
01:58:14,043 --> 01:58:18,376
Mother! Mother!

2690
01:58:19,584 --> 01:58:21,126
She is Zoya's daughter.

2691
01:58:21,334 --> 01:58:23,709
She lost her voice.

2692
01:58:24,668 --> 01:58:27,376
[emotional music]

2693
01:58:28,168 --> 01:58:29,834
Mother!

2694
01:58:30,543 --> 01:58:32,375
Don't kill them.
They are innocent.

2695
01:58:32,376 --> 01:58:34,376
They are clowns! Bloody clowns!

2696
01:58:36,209 --> 01:58:38,500
We're running away like cowards.

2697
01:58:38,501 --> 01:58:40,376
We'll at least be good human beings!

2698
01:58:40,501 --> 01:58:41,501
<i>Mother!</i>

2699
01:58:43,793 --> 01:58:45,251
I won't let any harm come
to this village.

2700
01:58:45,376 --> 01:58:47,251
I realised today what a coward you are.

2701
01:58:47,376 --> 01:58:50,751
Pilot... turn the helicopter around!

2702
01:58:51,084 --> 01:58:52,168
Let's go back!

2703
01:58:52,376 --> 01:58:53,501
Copy that.

2704
01:58:54,376 --> 01:58:57,876
[dramatic music]

2705
01:58:59,668 --> 01:59:02,918
[helicopter's sound]

2706
01:59:05,334 --> 01:59:09,667
- Once more...
- Give it all you got!

2707
01:59:09,668 --> 01:59:10,543
Come on.

2708
01:59:11,834 --> 01:59:14,751
[helicopter's sound]

2709
01:59:31,209 --> 01:59:34,251
[rapid gunshots]

2710
01:59:37,001 --> 01:59:39,001
[thud]

2711
01:59:42,543 --> 01:59:44,543
[upbeat music]

2712
01:59:45,084 --> 01:59:47,084
[rapid gunfire]

2713
01:59:47,376 --> 01:59:48,501
Everyone go there.

2714
01:59:50,084 --> 01:59:53,293
- [rapid gunfire continue]
- [upbeat music continues]

2715
01:59:57,501 --> 02:00:00,959
- [rapid gunfire continue]
- [upbeat music continues]

2716
02:00:02,084 --> 02:00:03,501
Hey, what are you doing?

2717
02:00:03,834 --> 02:00:05,834
- [head struck]
- [head struck]

2718
02:00:11,418 --> 02:00:13,918
- [gunshot]
- [thud]

2719
02:00:16,459 --> 02:00:18,459
[wall crashes]

2720
02:00:19,376 --> 02:00:21,458
[dramatic music]

2721
02:00:21,459 --> 02:00:23,459
[rapid gunfire]

2722
02:00:24,001 --> 02:00:25,043
Run.

2723
02:00:28,043 --> 02:00:29,584
Mother!

2724
02:00:29,793 --> 02:00:31,793
[emotional music]

2725
02:00:32,418 --> 02:00:33,334
Urvi.

2726
02:00:33,501 --> 02:00:34,750
- Urvi.
- Mother!

2727
02:00:34,751 --> 02:00:35,793
What did you say?

2728
02:00:36,209 --> 02:00:36,959
Mother!

2729
02:00:37,251 --> 02:00:38,417
Say it again.

2730
02:00:38,418 --> 02:00:39,293
Mother!

2731
02:00:40,293 --> 02:00:43,251
Urvi! Thank God!

2732
02:00:43,418 --> 02:00:45,418
[thud]

2733
02:00:45,626 --> 02:00:47,042
Come on.
Come on, Urvi!

2734
02:00:47,043 --> 02:00:49,125
- [rapid gunfire]
- [scream]

2735
02:00:49,126 --> 02:00:50,751
I want to tell you something.

2736
02:00:54,084 --> 02:00:55,543
Rajeev wasn't wrong.

2737
02:00:56,418 --> 02:00:59,167
<i>That night,
you two fell for Diya's ruse.</i>

2738
02:00:59,168 --> 02:01:02,418
<i>You wouldn't have believed Rajeev
if he had given clarification.</i>

2739
02:01:02,751 --> 02:01:04,293
You misunderstood him.

2740
02:01:07,001 --> 02:01:08,584
He's a good guy.

2741
02:01:09,876 --> 02:01:10,751
Go on.

2742
02:01:15,001 --> 02:01:16,168
Rajeev...

2743
02:01:16,918 --> 02:01:18,918
[heartwarming music]

2744
02:01:20,959 --> 02:01:22,959
[thud]

2745
02:01:24,251 --> 02:01:26,251
[heartwarming music continues]

2746
02:01:30,959 --> 02:01:32,168
You are not a cheater.

2747
02:01:33,668 --> 02:01:34,959
I am not a coward either.

2748
02:01:36,001 --> 02:01:37,043
Another thing...

2749
02:01:39,084 --> 02:01:40,793
you've put on weight.

2750
02:01:41,834 --> 02:01:43,375
[laughter]

2751
02:01:43,376 --> 02:01:45,000
Bro, get back up if you're done.

2752
02:01:45,001 --> 02:01:45,792
Or we're dead.

2753
02:01:45,793 --> 02:01:47,626
We've reunited after five years,

2754
02:01:47,793 --> 02:01:49,543
give me some time for romance.

2755
02:01:52,668 --> 02:01:54,209
Let's get out of here,
or we'll get killed.

2756
02:01:54,459 --> 02:01:56,376
- Let's go tell Zatara.
- Come on.

2757
02:01:57,918 --> 02:02:00,709
What about the villagers
you abandoned?

2758
02:02:02,418 --> 02:02:04,418
[emotional music]

2759
02:02:08,084 --> 02:02:09,168
Forgive me.

2760
02:02:10,084 --> 02:02:12,209
[gibberish]

2761
02:02:12,876 --> 02:02:14,376
[funny music]

2762
02:02:18,001 --> 02:02:18,876
Aunt...

2763
02:02:19,459 --> 02:02:20,709
Aunt is right.

2764
02:02:22,751 --> 02:02:24,251
How did he understand?

2765
02:02:25,209 --> 02:02:27,251
God knows what she's saying.

2766
02:02:27,793 --> 02:02:29,834
He didn't understand, by God.

2767
02:02:30,043 --> 02:02:31,168
O weeping mother...

2768
02:02:33,001 --> 02:02:34,626
Days of weeping have just begun...

2769
02:02:34,751 --> 02:02:35,667
For us?

2770
02:02:35,668 --> 02:02:36,668
For Zatara.

2771
02:02:38,626 --> 02:02:39,793
Don't worry, mother.

2772
02:02:40,793 --> 02:02:42,626
Zatara's that has started.

2773
02:02:44,626 --> 02:02:45,543
What's that?

2774
02:02:46,209 --> 02:02:47,418
That...

2775
02:02:47,543 --> 02:02:48,750
There he goes again.

2776
02:02:48,751 --> 02:02:50,543
We'll be done for
if he starts that again.

2777
02:02:50,709 --> 02:02:52,376
That's not the issue.

2778
02:02:52,584 --> 02:02:55,417
We have to free the people
of Azadganj.

2779
02:02:55,418 --> 02:02:56,709
- That's all.
- Right.

2780
02:02:56,876 --> 02:02:59,208
And we have to get these
villagers across the border.

2781
02:02:59,209 --> 02:02:59,667
Right.

2782
02:02:59,668 --> 02:03:01,625
We'll shoot anyone
who gets in the way?

2783
02:03:01,626 --> 02:03:04,333
We might not have weapons,
but we have courage.

2784
02:03:04,334 --> 02:03:04,959
Romeo's right.

2785
02:03:05,084 --> 02:03:07,543
Guys, guys, don't be crazy.

2786
02:03:07,709 --> 02:03:10,000
None of us will get out alive.

2787
02:03:10,001 --> 02:03:11,001
I have an idea.

2788
02:03:11,168 --> 02:03:13,083
We want weapons, not ideas.

2789
02:03:13,084 --> 02:03:17,334
I can take you to a place
where you can get weapons.

2790
02:03:17,459 --> 02:03:20,001
Zatara keeps all his weapons
in the warehouse nearby.

2791
02:03:20,209 --> 02:03:21,625
Then let's go there. Come on.

2792
02:03:21,626 --> 02:03:22,792
Let's go.

2793
02:03:22,793 --> 02:03:25,751
- Son.
- Come on, grandma. Let's go.

2794
02:03:25,959 --> 02:03:27,959
[door creaks]

2795
02:03:29,501 --> 02:03:31,459
This is it. Zatara's weapon.

2796
02:03:31,668 --> 02:03:33,418
- Take this.
- [music intensifies]

2797
02:03:34,459 --> 02:03:36,251
This is Zatara's warehouse.

2798
02:03:38,543 --> 02:03:41,376
- Are these real?
- These are not props!

2799
02:03:41,668 --> 02:03:43,250
Remington 700.

2800
02:03:43,251 --> 02:03:44,333
M-19.

2801
02:03:44,334 --> 02:03:45,626
Anna, what's that?

2802
02:03:45,751 --> 02:03:47,250
Leave that. Look at this.

2803
02:03:47,251 --> 02:03:51,126
I've used guns and bazookas in my life,
but nothing like this.

2804
02:03:51,251 --> 02:03:53,334
If this is beyond you,

2805
02:03:53,709 --> 02:03:55,376
then how will you fight Zatara?

2806
02:03:55,959 --> 02:03:58,293
Only the army can handle
weapons like this.

2807
02:03:58,793 --> 02:04:00,876
- Where will we get these army personnel?
- [thud]

2808
02:04:03,293 --> 02:04:06,084
- huh?
- [funny music]

2809
02:04:07,959 --> 02:04:11,334
Only the army can handle
weapons like this.

2810
02:04:12,668 --> 02:04:14,168
- Where will we get these army men--
- [thud]

2811
02:04:14,334 --> 02:04:15,126
Hey!

2812
02:04:15,543 --> 02:04:16,751
Are we doing comedy here?

2813
02:04:16,959 --> 02:04:17,917
Who made that sound?

2814
02:04:17,918 --> 02:04:19,918
- Was it you?-
- No! ummm.

2815
02:04:20,043 --> 02:04:22,168
Uncle... why are you
making that sound.

2816
02:04:22,293 --> 02:04:23,208
I haven't done anything.

2817
02:04:23,209 --> 02:04:24,334
Where is this sound coming from?

2818
02:04:24,626 --> 02:04:25,501
Down there.

2819
02:04:26,251 --> 02:04:27,750
But that's where pee comes from.

2820
02:04:27,751 --> 02:04:29,001
What behaviour is this?

2821
02:04:29,168 --> 02:04:30,668
Then where is the sound coming from?

2822
02:04:31,459 --> 02:04:33,834
The sound is coming
from somewhere here.

2823
02:04:34,626 --> 02:04:36,376
Move it.

2824
02:04:36,584 --> 02:04:37,876
Get a tool.

2825
02:04:38,043 --> 02:04:39,543
Let me handle it.
It's not your cup of tea.

2826
02:04:41,293 --> 02:04:43,459
- What are you doing?
- [thud]

2827
02:04:43,626 --> 02:04:44,792
Idiot, aim the other way.

2828
02:04:44,793 --> 02:04:45,876
Alright, fine.

2829
02:04:46,126 --> 02:04:47,750
[thud]

2830
02:04:47,751 --> 02:04:49,709
- It's done.
- Stop. Stop.

2831
02:04:50,084 --> 02:04:52,084
[chain rattles]

2832
02:04:52,459 --> 02:04:53,626
Lift it. Lift it. Come on.

2833
02:04:56,293 --> 02:04:57,292
What is happening?

2834
02:04:57,293 --> 02:04:58,168
Tunnel?

2835
02:04:58,876 --> 02:05:00,334
[thud]

2836
02:05:02,459 --> 02:05:04,459
[music intensifies]

2837
02:05:07,251 --> 02:05:09,251
[dramatic music]

2838
02:05:11,834 --> 02:05:15,043
[dramatic music continues]

2839
02:05:18,168 --> 02:05:21,334
[dramatic music continues]

2840
02:05:24,793 --> 02:05:28,334
[dramatic music continues]

2841
02:05:34,876 --> 02:05:36,501
Indian Army?

2842
02:05:37,084 --> 02:05:37,876
You...

2843
02:05:39,084 --> 02:05:40,292
are also from army?

2844
02:05:40,293 --> 02:05:41,668
[funny music]

2845
02:05:42,584 --> 02:05:44,500
I'll join if you want me to, sir.

2846
02:05:44,501 --> 02:05:45,458
Who are all of you?

2847
02:05:45,459 --> 02:05:46,709
And why are you here?

2848
02:05:46,876 --> 02:05:48,793
- To shoot.
- Who?

2849
02:05:49,084 --> 02:05:51,125
Anyone who messes with us.
We'll kill him.

2850
02:05:51,126 --> 02:05:53,209
We're actors.
We came here to shoot a film.

2851
02:05:53,334 --> 02:05:55,542
We got stuck here because of Zatara.

2852
02:05:55,543 --> 02:05:56,959
But who are you guys?

2853
02:05:57,126 --> 02:05:58,918
We're the Indian Army.

2854
02:06:01,668 --> 02:06:03,293
I am Brigadier Karan.

2855
02:06:03,459 --> 02:06:05,626
I am Lieutenant Colonel Arjun.

2856
02:06:05,834 --> 02:06:07,668
Then you must be Duryodhan?

2857
02:06:09,793 --> 02:06:11,876
Arjun, Karan, Duryodhan.

2858
02:06:12,293 --> 02:06:13,543
<i>Mahabharat?</i>

2859
02:06:16,209 --> 02:06:22,084
♪ Mahabharat TV show theme song plays ♪

2860
02:06:22,626 --> 02:06:27,918
♪ Mahabharat TV show theme song continues ♪

2861
02:06:28,168 --> 02:06:29,834
- ♪ Mahabha-- ♪
- [funny sound]

2862
02:06:33,376 --> 02:06:36,251
Zatara held us captive
here for 15 years.

2863
02:06:37,126 --> 02:06:38,543
Us and the general.

2864
02:06:38,876 --> 02:06:40,168
General?

2865
02:06:40,334 --> 02:06:42,709
- Where is the General?
- [thud]

2866
02:06:46,459 --> 02:06:49,168
[dramatic music]

2867
02:06:52,084 --> 02:06:54,626
[dramatic music continues]

2868
02:06:58,334 --> 02:07:01,168
[dramatic music continues]

2869
02:07:03,543 --> 02:07:07,043
[dramatic music continues]

2870
02:07:10,334 --> 02:07:12,793
[dramatic music continues]

2871
02:07:15,418 --> 02:07:18,334
[dramatic music continues]

2872
02:07:19,084 --> 02:07:21,084
And he's our General sir.

2873
02:07:22,001 --> 02:07:23,209
Vishwajeet Kohli.

2874
02:07:23,626 --> 02:07:25,750
Major Vishwajeet Raj Kohli.

2875
02:07:25,751 --> 02:07:28,376
He went on a mission
for India one day.

2876
02:07:28,709 --> 02:07:30,918
He's been missing
in action for 15 years.

2877
02:07:33,251 --> 02:07:35,251
[dramatic music continues]

2878
02:07:37,626 --> 02:07:39,918
[dramatic music continues]

2879
02:07:43,084 --> 02:07:45,709
[dramatic music continues]

2880
02:07:46,251 --> 02:07:48,001
They both look that...

2881
02:07:48,168 --> 02:07:48,917
Sweet dish.

2882
02:07:48,918 --> 02:07:51,084
No... like those in films like
Ram and Shyam.

2883
02:07:52,043 --> 02:07:54,459
- He's talking about double role.
- Yes.

2884
02:07:56,209 --> 02:07:57,042
Father.

2885
02:07:57,043 --> 02:07:58,001
Father?

2886
02:07:58,209 --> 02:07:59,293
He's his father.

2887
02:08:02,751 --> 02:08:03,834
[speaks indistinctly] Rajeev.

2888
02:08:05,834 --> 02:08:06,793
My son.

2889
02:08:06,918 --> 02:08:07,792
[funny music]

2890
02:08:07,793 --> 02:08:10,001
I am so happy to see you.

2891
02:08:11,293 --> 02:08:12,543
The apple of my eye.

2892
02:08:13,668 --> 02:08:15,293
My darling son.

2893
02:08:15,626 --> 02:08:16,417
son?

2894
02:08:16,418 --> 02:08:18,043
My darling son.

2895
02:08:18,501 --> 02:08:20,000
What language is he speaking?

2896
02:08:20,001 --> 02:08:21,418
Father, you're lisping?

2897
02:08:21,668 --> 02:08:23,668
[funny music continues]

2898
02:08:23,834 --> 02:08:24,834
Yeth, son.

2899
02:08:25,626 --> 02:08:27,626
I raised my voice in
front of enemies,

2900
02:08:28,418 --> 02:08:30,293
and they cut off my tongue.

2901
02:08:30,418 --> 02:08:34,584
[speaks in urdu]

2902
02:08:34,793 --> 02:08:36,793
[gibberish]

2903
02:08:37,709 --> 02:08:40,250
Zatara didn't cut her tongue
which he should have,

2904
02:08:40,251 --> 02:08:42,084
but he cut off the poor
general's tongue.

2905
02:08:44,043 --> 02:08:45,084
And his too.

2906
02:08:45,293 --> 02:08:46,959
Since then, I've been lisping.

2907
02:08:47,543 --> 02:08:49,668
[speaks indistinctly] All day I call a gun a bun.

2908
02:08:49,918 --> 02:08:51,459
Gun powder... bun powder

2909
02:08:51,584 --> 02:08:54,209
More so, I call the nations
soil nations toil.

2910
02:08:54,418 --> 02:08:57,501
Enough, father.
I cannot tolerate this anymore.

2911
02:08:58,001 --> 02:09:00,708
The less you speak, the better.

2912
02:09:00,709 --> 02:09:01,709
Enough.

2913
02:09:02,959 --> 02:09:05,626
Son... things will only be better

2914
02:09:06,751 --> 02:09:10,418
when we can set Azadganj free.

2915
02:09:10,959 --> 02:09:12,293
My brave warriors.

2916
02:09:12,418 --> 02:09:14,334
[speaks indistinctly]

2917
02:09:15,459 --> 02:09:16,334
But now

2918
02:09:17,293 --> 02:09:19,168
We'll have fun in jungle now.

2919
02:09:19,793 --> 02:09:20,958
it'th time for a showdown.

2920
02:09:20,959 --> 02:09:21,876
Excuse me, uncle.

2921
02:09:22,001 --> 02:09:22,958
What do you want to say?

2922
02:09:22,959 --> 02:09:26,583
We didn't understand a word you said.

2923
02:09:26,584 --> 02:09:28,834
Explain the meaning of any one. Enough.

2924
02:09:30,293 --> 02:09:32,793
jungle was all fun and games...

2925
02:09:33,084 --> 02:09:35,043
But general sir is trying to say,

2926
02:09:35,209 --> 02:09:37,501
now it's time for a showdown.

2927
02:09:37,626 --> 02:09:39,251
Got it.

2928
02:09:39,418 --> 02:09:40,334
Welcome...

2929
02:09:40,501 --> 02:09:42,209
Welcome to the Jungle.

2930
02:09:42,376 --> 02:09:44,293
[speak indistinctly] Welcome to the Jungle.

2931
02:09:44,418 --> 02:09:46,168
You're making fun of me.

2932
02:09:46,293 --> 02:09:47,251
No...

2933
02:09:47,501 --> 02:09:50,793
Welcome To The Jungle.

2934
02:09:50,959 --> 02:09:57,959
Welcome To The Jungle.

2935
02:09:58,376 --> 02:10:00,334
[clear voice] Those soldiers attacked us.

2936
02:10:00,501 --> 02:10:02,334
And also seized our weapons.

2937
02:10:03,001 --> 02:10:05,959
[dramatic music]

2938
02:10:11,001 --> 02:10:13,043
[speaks indistinctly] Hello. Indian Army calling.

2939
02:10:13,293 --> 02:10:14,959
<i>Indian Army calling.</i>

2940
02:10:15,834 --> 02:10:17,793
[clear voice] Hello. Major Vikrant Bakshi here.

2941
02:10:17,959 --> 02:10:20,250
This is General Vishwajeet
Kohli speaking.

2942
02:10:20,251 --> 02:10:22,876
Which child got hold
of this radio frequency?

2943
02:10:23,084 --> 02:10:25,084
[laughter]

2944
02:10:26,168 --> 02:10:27,333
Let me speak.
He's my father.

2945
02:10:27,334 --> 02:10:32,168
The person you were talking
to was our General Vishwajeet Kohli.

2946
02:10:33,334 --> 02:10:34,168
Vishwajeet Kohli.

2947
02:10:34,293 --> 02:10:35,750
He's the guy who has been missing
for several years.

2948
02:10:35,751 --> 02:10:37,084
- Give me the phone, please.
- Yes, sir.

2949
02:10:38,459 --> 02:10:40,418
This is General Avinash Singh here.

2950
02:10:40,584 --> 02:10:43,459
<i>It's an honour.
You are a living legend, sir.</i>

2951
02:10:43,584 --> 02:10:45,168
We've heard about your feats.

2952
02:10:45,293 --> 02:10:47,418
We've escaped Zatara's captivity.

2953
02:10:47,668 --> 02:10:50,709
And we want to help the people
of Azadganj cross the border.

2954
02:10:50,834 --> 02:10:52,083
<i>It's great news
that you guys are free.</i>

2955
02:10:52,084 --> 02:10:53,418
[speaks indistinctly] Do you want to say something?

2956
02:10:53,709 --> 02:10:54,959
[clear voice] I am proud of you.

2957
02:10:55,209 --> 02:10:55,959
Azadganj?

2958
02:10:56,084 --> 02:10:58,917
Isn't this the same village
whose people Zatara took hostage?

2959
02:10:58,918 --> 02:11:02,834
We'll pass through the jungle
from Azadganj to reach the border.

2960
02:11:02,959 --> 02:11:06,251
But sir, the border is three
kilometres from Azadganj.

2961
02:11:06,376 --> 02:11:08,459
<i>- There's dense jungle in the way.</i>
- You're crazy. Give him the walkie.

2962
02:11:08,626 --> 02:11:10,208
Only after that will you
reach the border.

2963
02:11:10,209 --> 02:11:11,543
Don't worry.

2964
02:11:11,834 --> 02:11:13,168
We'll get there.

2965
02:11:13,376 --> 02:11:16,251
And we'll be there in... two minutes.

2966
02:11:17,959 --> 02:11:19,500
Zero. Zero.

2967
02:11:19,501 --> 02:11:20,543
Twenty minutes.

2968
02:11:20,751 --> 02:11:22,500
As soon as we leave,

2969
02:11:22,501 --> 02:11:25,293
you call an air strike
on Zatara and the jungle.

2970
02:11:25,418 --> 02:11:28,667
Turn the entire place into
a grave with target bombing.

2971
02:11:28,668 --> 02:11:30,709
But, sir,
if there's even a slight delay,

2972
02:11:30,834 --> 02:11:33,126
then your lives could be in danger.

2973
02:11:35,209 --> 02:11:37,292
There won't be any delay.

2974
02:11:37,293 --> 02:11:39,584
You have Vishwajeet Kohli's word!

2975
02:11:40,001 --> 02:11:43,209
And once Kohli gives his word,
there's no taking it back.

2976
02:11:43,834 --> 02:11:45,584
The man's got no tongue.
How's he supposed to give his word?

2977
02:11:46,334 --> 02:11:47,458
Hey...

2978
02:11:47,459 --> 02:11:48,500
General sir. General sir.

2979
02:11:48,501 --> 02:11:52,334
He's saying that even if
our heads are chopped off,

2980
02:11:52,459 --> 02:11:53,833
even if it costs us our lives,

2981
02:11:53,834 --> 02:11:56,168
we'll say Welcome.

2982
02:11:56,334 --> 02:11:57,876
To the Jungle!

2983
02:12:01,793 --> 02:12:04,501
[explosions]

2984
02:12:06,793 --> 02:12:07,375
Tell me.

2985
02:12:07,376 --> 02:12:10,083
Zatara... they blew up our weapons

2986
02:12:10,084 --> 02:12:12,000
and released the soldiers
we held captive for 15 years.

2987
02:12:12,001 --> 02:12:13,750
Now they are helping them.

2988
02:12:13,751 --> 02:12:15,126
Which way are they headed?

2989
02:12:15,293 --> 02:12:16,793
They are headed towards the border.

2990
02:12:16,918 --> 02:12:18,668
Kill them. Kill them all.

2991
02:12:19,084 --> 02:12:21,084
- [horses galloping]
- [horses neighing]

2992
02:12:21,209 --> 02:12:23,209
[cars racing]

2993
02:12:24,543 --> 02:12:26,543
[intense music]

2994
02:12:26,793 --> 02:12:29,834
- [rapid gunfire]
- [horses galloping]

2995
02:12:31,459 --> 02:12:34,293
[rapid gunfire continues]

2996
02:12:36,959 --> 02:12:38,959
[rapid gunfire continues]

2997
02:12:39,209 --> 02:12:42,751
[explosion]

2998
02:12:45,251 --> 02:12:46,125
No, no.

2999
02:12:46,126 --> 02:12:47,418
- Anna.
- Rajeev.

3000
02:12:47,543 --> 02:12:48,501
Father!

3001
02:12:53,209 --> 02:12:55,459
- [dramatic music]
- [glass breaks]

3002
02:12:56,626 --> 02:12:58,668
[explosion]

3003
02:13:01,418 --> 02:13:02,001
Come on.

3004
02:13:02,168 --> 02:13:03,625
May you have the years meant for me?

3005
02:13:03,626 --> 02:13:05,459
This is no time for coddling.

3006
02:13:06,043 --> 02:13:07,543
Come on. Everyone go.

3007
02:13:09,668 --> 02:13:12,084
Come on, let's go.

3008
02:13:14,084 --> 02:13:16,084
[intense music]

3009
02:13:17,626 --> 02:13:18,959
Sir, air base.

3010
02:13:19,334 --> 02:13:21,334
[warship approaches]

3011
02:13:23,959 --> 02:13:26,458
I want all aircraft
to be lined up immediately.

3012
02:13:26,459 --> 02:13:28,334
<i>Copy that, sir.
Move the aircraft.</i>

3013
02:13:28,584 --> 02:13:30,250
We have only 18 minutes.

3014
02:13:30,251 --> 02:13:31,542
That's an order!

3015
02:13:31,543 --> 02:13:33,543
- [gunshot]
- [scream]

3016
02:13:34,668 --> 02:13:36,668
[emotional music]

3017
02:13:37,376 --> 02:13:38,376
Karan.

3018
02:13:39,376 --> 02:13:42,209
[intense music]

3019
02:13:44,209 --> 02:13:46,042
- [gunshot]
- [rapid gunfire]

3020
02:13:46,043 --> 02:13:48,043
[explosion]

3021
02:13:49,543 --> 02:13:51,959
[engines roar]
- [horses galloping]

3022
02:13:55,793 --> 02:13:59,668
- [indistinct crowd chatter]
- Hey, hey, hey!

3023
02:14:04,334 --> 02:14:05,958
We're caught between a well
and a ravine.

3024
02:14:05,959 --> 02:14:07,084
Where's the well?

3025
02:14:08,001 --> 02:14:09,750
Hang on. Where is the ravine?

3026
02:14:09,751 --> 02:14:10,918
Over here.

3027
02:14:11,293 --> 02:14:13,293
- [horses galloping]
- [horses neighing]

3028
02:14:16,834 --> 02:14:20,918
Look... we have to do
what every brave person does.

3029
02:14:21,043 --> 02:14:22,001
What?

3030
02:14:22,168 --> 02:14:23,959
We... have to hide.

3031
02:14:24,084 --> 02:14:26,293
- Hide. Hide.
- [crowd noise]

3032
02:14:27,584 --> 02:14:29,751
- [horses galloping]
- [horses neighing]

3033
02:14:33,251 --> 02:14:35,250
[gunshots]

3034
02:14:35,251 --> 02:14:38,001
[rapid gunfire]

3035
02:14:43,043 --> 02:14:45,043
[rapid gunfire continues]

3036
02:14:46,001 --> 02:14:49,084
[upbeat music]

3037
02:14:53,709 --> 02:14:56,876
- [upbeat music continues]
- [gunshot]

3038
02:14:59,084 --> 02:15:01,084
[breathing heavily]

3039
02:15:01,334 --> 02:15:03,334
[cheering]

3040
02:15:07,043 --> 02:15:10,334
We'll become easy targets
if we stay together.

3041
02:15:10,459 --> 02:15:11,875
We'll all die.

3042
02:15:11,876 --> 02:15:14,209
Yes, let's separate
and meet at the border.

3043
02:15:14,334 --> 02:15:16,834
He's right.
We'll meet at the border.

3044
02:15:17,043 --> 02:15:18,709
Alright. Let's go.

3045
02:15:18,959 --> 02:15:21,334
<i>Chief, a lot of our men are dead.</i>

3046
02:15:21,501 --> 02:15:22,918
<i>It's getting difficult
to stop them.</i>

3047
02:15:24,793 --> 02:15:26,793
[intense music]

3048
02:15:31,126 --> 02:15:33,126
[intense music continues]

3049
02:15:36,168 --> 02:15:37,833
Who's over there, idiot?

3050
02:15:37,834 --> 02:15:38,959
Fall in line.

3051
02:15:39,251 --> 02:15:40,709
Follow me, everyone.

3052
02:15:42,168 --> 02:15:44,168
[tense music]

3053
02:15:45,501 --> 02:15:47,501
- Hey, terrorist?
- Yes, sir.

3054
02:15:47,626 --> 02:15:49,626
- [gunshots]
- [screams]

3055
02:15:51,501 --> 02:15:53,626
You would have been dead
if you had gone any further.

3056
02:15:53,834 --> 02:15:54,626
Come on.

3057
02:15:55,709 --> 02:15:57,833
[rapid gunfire]

3058
02:15:57,834 --> 02:15:59,918
- [screams]
- [engines roar]

3059
02:16:00,251 --> 02:16:03,293
- [rapid gunfire]
- [engines roar]

3060
02:16:07,043 --> 02:16:10,084
- [action music]
- [gunshots]

3061
02:16:13,001 --> 02:16:15,001
[engines roar]

3062
02:16:16,918 --> 02:16:17,709
Let's go.

3063
02:16:19,418 --> 02:16:21,418
[rapid gunfire]

3064
02:16:23,459 --> 02:16:26,167
[upbeat music]

3065
02:16:26,168 --> 02:16:28,168
[screams]

3066
02:16:28,334 --> 02:16:29,917
- [rapid gunfire]
- [horses neighing]

3067
02:16:29,918 --> 02:16:31,918
[screams]

3068
02:16:34,043 --> 02:16:36,043
[playful music]

3069
02:16:37,209 --> 02:16:38,418
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

3070
02:16:39,501 --> 02:16:41,501
- [thud]
- [scream]

3071
02:16:43,334 --> 02:16:45,334
[action music]

3072
02:16:46,668 --> 02:16:48,668
[rapid gunfire]

3073
02:16:50,251 --> 02:16:52,251
- [fight]
- [upbeat music]

3074
02:16:55,584 --> 02:16:56,626
Who are you guys?

3075
02:16:57,043 --> 02:16:58,084
Where do you come from?

3076
02:16:58,209 --> 02:16:59,334
Why do you come?

3077
02:17:00,543 --> 02:17:02,543
[rapid gunfire]

3078
02:17:05,084 --> 02:17:07,084
[upbeat music]

3079
02:17:07,626 --> 02:17:09,626
- [gunshot]
- [explosion]

3080
02:17:11,751 --> 02:17:13,751
[dramatic music]

3081
02:17:14,001 --> 02:17:15,333
[whooping]

3082
02:17:15,334 --> 02:17:16,334
Hurry up, boys.

3083
02:17:16,459 --> 02:17:18,459
We have only 15 minutes.

3084
02:17:23,543 --> 02:17:25,083
[rapid gunfire]

3085
02:17:25,084 --> 02:17:26,543
Nainsukh, give me bullets.

3086
02:17:26,668 --> 02:17:27,584
Take it. Take it.

3087
02:17:27,709 --> 02:17:29,542
What am I supposed to do,
hang them one by one?

3088
02:17:29,543 --> 02:17:30,167
Give me bullets.

3089
02:17:30,168 --> 02:17:31,333
I gave you a gun.
Shoot them.

3090
02:17:31,334 --> 02:17:32,167
Why will you hang them?

3091
02:17:32,168 --> 02:17:33,750
[fight]

3092
02:17:33,751 --> 02:17:34,667
Give me something.

3093
02:17:34,668 --> 02:17:36,708
Here. Empty the whole magazine.

3094
02:17:36,709 --> 02:17:38,626
What is this?
A lunch date?

3095
02:17:39,376 --> 02:17:40,584
- Look at me.
- [thud]

3096
02:17:42,001 --> 02:17:43,458
Romeo. Someone's hitting me.

3097
02:17:43,459 --> 02:17:44,542
Romeo's hitting you.

3098
02:17:44,543 --> 02:17:45,543
Come on, or we'll all die.

3099
02:17:45,793 --> 02:17:48,001
[rapid gunfire]
- [thud]

3100
02:17:48,751 --> 02:17:51,751
- [sad music]
- Oh Lord...

3101
02:17:52,793 --> 02:17:55,293
You have to shoot them, not get shot.

3102
02:17:55,501 --> 02:17:56,375
Get the stretcher.

3103
02:17:56,376 --> 02:17:57,458
Look where you are shooting.

3104
02:17:57,459 --> 02:17:58,376
Are you blind?

3105
02:17:58,709 --> 02:18:00,209
The stretcher's here, brother.
Lie down.

3106
02:18:00,334 --> 02:18:02,334
[action music]

3107
02:18:03,584 --> 02:18:05,751
[action music continues]

3108
02:18:09,001 --> 02:18:09,958
Don't lift that thing,

3109
02:18:09,959 --> 02:18:11,167
or you'll get crushed under it.

3110
02:18:11,168 --> 02:18:12,334
Don is here. Don is here.

3111
02:18:12,459 --> 02:18:14,459
[rapid gunfire]

3112
02:18:14,709 --> 02:18:15,751
I love it.

3113
02:18:16,709 --> 02:18:18,709
[explosion]

3114
02:18:18,918 --> 02:18:20,918
[rapid gunfire]

3115
02:18:21,168 --> 02:18:23,584
- Take this.
- [funny music]

3116
02:18:24,001 --> 02:18:26,001
[fire blazing]

3117
02:18:27,501 --> 02:18:29,501
[screams]

3118
02:18:31,001 --> 02:18:32,918
What is this item, Anna?

3119
02:18:33,043 --> 02:18:34,376
It's flower. Flower.

3120
02:18:34,543 --> 02:18:38,043
- Yeah... it won't bloody douse.
- It's Anna's firepower.

3121
02:18:40,376 --> 02:18:42,418
Jai Bhawani
(Glory to Goddess Bhawani).

3122
02:18:43,001 --> 02:18:44,792
- Did you throw the grenade?
- Yes, I did.

3123
02:18:44,793 --> 02:18:46,084
Then why didn't it explode?

3124
02:18:46,501 --> 02:18:47,083
I don't know.

3125
02:18:47,084 --> 02:18:49,543
- Fake stuff.
- Guess it's a dud.

3126
02:18:49,709 --> 02:18:51,834
Sir... we cannot get

3127
02:18:51,959 --> 02:18:54,043
the villagers across the border
in such a short time.

3128
02:18:54,168 --> 02:18:55,584
We have to buy some time, sir.

3129
02:18:55,959 --> 02:18:57,000
[speaks indistinctly] Give me the walkie-talkie.

3130
02:18:57,001 --> 02:18:57,918
Walkie-talkie?

3131
02:18:58,126 --> 02:18:59,125
But we don't have it.

3132
02:18:59,126 --> 02:19:00,084
General Kohli?

3133
02:19:00,751 --> 02:19:01,751
General Kohli?

3134
02:19:01,876 --> 02:19:04,459
General Kohli,
come in, please.

3135
02:19:05,418 --> 02:19:06,793
Why aren't they answering?

